window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS=(window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":151,"title":"Chapter 151: Buer","paragraphs":["Morgana moved through the forest like something that had decided the trees were an inconvenience rather than an obstacle.","Her figure blurred between the trunks, covering ground at a speed that left the undergrowth swaying in her wake long after she had already passed through it.","Her sky-blue hair had come partially loose from its bun and streamed behind her. Her amethyst eyes were fixed forward, cold and completely focused.","She had already sent word to the other instructors.","Pull every student out of the forest. All of them, from every direction, as fast as possible.","She hadn’t explained in detail. There wasn’t time for detail. The urgency in her message had been enough.","Now she was running toward the last known position of the vanished signals.","She kept her expression controlled, the way she always did. But underneath it, the worry was real and her heart was shaking slightly.","Damien’s signal was among the missing.","Her disciple. Her responsibility in a way that went beyond the standard instructor relationship.","She had taken him on personally, trained him directly, invested in his development with genuine intent. If something had happened to him.","And Noah as well.","She hadn’t expected to feel anything particular about that.","He was a student. Capable and unusual in ways she was still working out. Yet she had felt it when his signal disappeared.","A tightening somewhere between and professional that she was currently not examining.","He was the only student who openly asked for training and spar with her.","She pushed more mana into her legs and went faster.","The trees thinned slightly ahead where the terrain changed around a cluster of old rock formations.","And Morgana vaulted a fallen trunk without breaking stride, her coat snapping behind her from the speed.","She was close.","Then something dropped from the canopy above and landed in the path directly in front of her.","She stopped.","Not slowly. Instantly, the way only someone with complete control of their own momentum could stop. One moment moving, the next completely still, three meters from the figure that had landed in her way.","He straightened from the landing crouch and looked at her.","Dark hair cut to the jaw. Dark blue eyes with vertical pupils that caught the filtered forest light in a way that human eyes didn’t.","The cloak he was wearing settled around him as he rose, and the ease with which he had dropped from that height and simply stood up said everything about what he was.","Demon. And not a weak one.","\"Morgana Celestine,\" he said pleasantly, like they were being introduced at a social gathering. \"My name is Buel. \"","He inclined his head in a greeting that was almost courteous.","Morgana looked at him.","\"Demon...tell me...the students,\" she said, her voice even and very cold. \"You’re responsible for their disappearance, aren’t you?.\"","Buer smiled. It reached his eyes that made it worse rather than better.","\"I took a few of them, yes.\" He tilted his head slightly.","\"It isn’t as serious as you’re making it. They’re not dead... well. Most of them aren’t.\" He let that sit for exactly the right amount of time to be unpleasant.","\"My suggestion would be to turn around and go back to the students you still have. The ones who are safe. Cut your losses, as they say. We are just taking few.\"","The mana that came off Morgana’s body wasn’t a gradual build.","It detonated outward from her all at once. A single pressure wave of dense, dark energy that rolled through the surrounding forest in every direction simultaneously.","The trees nearest to her groaned from it. Undergrowth flattened outward in a ring.","Birds that had been sitting in branches fifty meters away launched themselves into the sky in a panicked mass.","The air around her darkened at the edges, her mana carrying the particular quality of her affinity.","Not the clean sharp darkness of absence but something deeper and more dangerous, the kind of dark that had destruction and weight in it.","Her amethyst eyes had shifted to a deep, deep purple.","Bael looked at the display with genuine interest rather than fear, which told her something important about him.","\"No wish to stand down,\" he said. \"Understood then... you people really love to work hard..coukd have save lot of effort if you had just back away.\"","He reached beneath his cloak and drew two swords simultaneously.","One in each hand, long and well-maintained, the blades carried by someone who used them constantly rather than occasionally.","The moment they cleared their sheaths, the dark blue energy started. It didn’t gather like mana did– it rose from him like heat, coating both blades in a layer.","That was simultaneously sharp and heavy, the edges of the aura crackling faintly where it compressed most densely.","Morgana’s eyes narrowed by a fraction.","It was Aura.","Not many fighters used it. The discipline required to compress mana into a sustained external coating of that density was considerable.","It demanded either a specific talent for it or years of focused practice, usually both.","One saw it in dedicated weapon practitioners, pure martial artists, people who had chosen one path and walked it until the path ran out.","Buer held both blades with the relaxed grip of someone who had been doing this for a very long time.","She reached into her storage ring.","The spear that came out was black. Not dark grey, not charcoal, but a true unreflective black that seemed to pull the light around it. Slightly inward rather than bounce it back.","It was long and well-balanced in her grip, and the moment her hand closed around the shaft. The darkness mana she was already releasing began to orient toward it naturally, like it recognized the weapon.","Buer looked at the spear and something in his expression became more serious.","\"Astral core....that means an S rank,\" he said quietly. More to himself than to her. He could guess her power just by feeling her mana.","Morgana didn’t respond to that.","She raised her free hand and the air in front of her changed.","Magic circles appeared. Not one, not two, but a cascade of them materializing in overlapping layers across the space between her and Bael.","Each one was different, rotating at its own speed, the inscriptions on their surfaces dense with the particular complexity.","That came from someone who had been casting for so long that what others needed to construct. One step at a time she could place simultaneously without visible effort.","Multi-cast.","Six circles. All darkness affinity. All charged and waiting.","The forest around them had gone very quiet. Even the wind seemed to have decided to stay out of this particular stretch of trees.","Buer looked at the circles, then at Morgana, then shifted his stance. Feet wider, both blades coming up, the aura on them intensifying until the dark blue coating crackled audibly.","Morgana’s expression didn’t change.","Her grip on the black spear tightened once.","\"Where are my students?\"","Buer smiled again, though it was a different smile than before. This one had respect underneath it, which was the most honest thing he had shown her so far.","\"Somewhere you won’t reach in time,\" he said.","The aura on his blades flared.","Morgana moved first."]},{"number":152,"title":"Chapter 152: Stalling Time","paragraphs":["Morgana moved first. She thrust her black spear forward.","At the same time, the six magic circles floating around her lit up. They activated one after another exactly as she had planned.","The first circle collapsed and released a powerful attack.","A thick spike of darkness mana shot through the forest. It wasn’t a beam or a wave. It was something much denser.","The attack struck the ground where Buer had been standing.","BOOM!","The impact blasted apart the earth and left a large crater behind.","But Buer had already moved. He jumped to the side with both swords raised. Dark blue aura covered his blades.","The second spell came immediately after the first. This one was a large curved slash of darkness energy.","Morgana had aimed it to follow his movement.","Buer swung one of his swords and deflected it.The attack flew off course and crashed into the trees nearby.","Several giant trees were instantly destroyed.","Their upper halves disappeared in a burst of black energy before crashing to the ground.","The third magic circle activated. This attack was different. No projectile appeared. Instead, a huge pressure suddenly descended from above.","It felt as if an invisible mountain had been dropped onto that part of the forest.","The ground cracked. Then the earth sank.","Tree roots were ripped from the soil. Buer crossed both swords above his head.","The pressure slammed into him. His knees bent. His boots sank into the ground. The dark blue aura around his weapons burned brightly as he resisted the spell.","A growl escaped his mouth.","Then he pushed back. The pressure finally broke apart. The moment it disappeared, Buer exploded forward.","He shot out of the crater and rushed directly toward Morgana.","Both swords came down in a powerful overhead strike. The attack was aimed straight at her.","Morgana did not step backward. She stepped sideways. Her black spear rose horizontally.","CLANG!","The spear blocked both swords at once. The collision shook the entire area. A powerful shockwave spread outward.","Leaves were ripped from every nearby tree. A visible ring of wind rolled across the forest floor.","For a moment, neither of them moved. Buer pushed down with both swords. Dark blue aura crackled around his blades. Morgana pushed darkness mana into her spear.","The two energies clashed against each other. Neither side gained an advantage. Then the fourth magic circle activated behind Morgana.","Buer immediately sensed the danger. \"Damn!\"","He jumped backward before the spell could fully form.","A second later, the spell exploded where he had been standing. A huge sphere of compressed darkness expanded outward.","Everything inside a thirty-meter area vanished.","Be it trees, bushes or grass. All of it disappeared. Only a massive black depression remained in the earth.","Buer landed roughly thirty meters away.","Thud","The moment his feet touched the ground, he charged again.","This time his movement changed. He was faster and less predictable. He didn’t run in a straight line.","Instead, he moved between trees, changing direction constantly. The remaining magic circles would have a much harder time targeting him that way.","Morgana followed his movements carefully. Her eyes never left him.","The fifth magic circle activated.She didn’t aim at where Buer currently was. She aimed where she predicted he would be.","Buer noticed the attack at the last moment. He kicked off a tree trunk and changed direction.","But he wasn’t fast enough. The spell struck his shoulder.","BOOM!","The explosion was enormous. The entire section of forest erupted. Trees were thrown into the air. Massive trunks spun through the sky before crashing back down.","The sound was deafening.","A giant crater formed where the attack landed. Smoke and dust filled the area. For several seconds, nothing could be seen.","Morgana stood near the edge of the destruction. Her black spear remained pointed forward.","The sixth magic circle floated behind her, still ready to fire.","She watched the smoke carefully. Then she saw a blue light moving inside it.","Buer walked out. His cloak was gone. The explosion had completely destroyed it.","His coat underneath was heavily damaged. His left shoulder and part of his chest were exposed.","The skin there was burned badly. One of his swords now had a visible crack running through the blade.","The aura around his weapons had weakened. Blood ran down the side of his face from a cut above his eye.","Buer looked down at his injuries. Then he looked back at Morgana.\"That one landed,\" he said.","His voice remained calm despite his injuries.He rotated his damaged shoulder once.","Then he raised both swords again.","\"You are exactly what they say you are.\"","Morgana didn’t answer. The sixth magic circle activated. A powerful darkness attack rushed toward Buer. It was like a wave of darkness.","Instead of dodging, Buer attacked. He thrust both swords forward. The dark blue aura around his blades exploded outward.","Two massive arcs of energy shot forward. The attacks collided head-on.","The explosion was bigger than any of the previous ones.","The blast shot upward into the sky. Darkness mana and blue aura mixed together.","The force tore through the forest canopy above them. Trees were flattened in every direction. The ground trembled violently.","When the energy finally disappeared, both of them were still standing.","The forest around them was almost unrecognizable.","Huge craters covered the area. Countless trees had fallen. Large sections of the ground were scorched black.","The canopy overhead had been completely destroyed. Sunlight now poured down from the open sky above.","The place no longer looked like a forest. It looked like a battlefield after a natural disaster.","Buer was breathing harder now. The crack in his sword had become larger.","His burned shoulder was clearly affecting his movements.","Morgana wasn’t unharmed either. Blood dripped from the hand holding her spear. The shockwave from the last collision had injured her grip.","Her hair had completely come loose.","Several small cuts covered her arms from flying debris.","They stood facing each other across the ruined battlefield.","Neither had fallen. Neither had backed down. For a few moments, silence filled the area.","Then Morgana finally spoke. \"You’re not here to fight me.\"","Her voice was calm. Even with blood running down her hand.\"If you were, you would have gone all out already.\"","Her eyes narrowed. \"You’re stalling.\"","Buer remained silent. A few seconds passed. Then a small smile appeared on his face.","This smile looked more genuine than the confident grin he had worn before.","\"You noticed.\"","Morgana’s expression darkened. Her grip tightened around the black spear. The pressure around her seemed to grow colder.","\"Where,\" she asked quietly, \"are my students?\"","The smile slowly disappeared from Buer’s face. The small ruined part of forest fell silent once again."]},{"number":153,"title":"Chapter 153: Fight For Survival Continued","paragraphs":["Damien could not use his strongest ability. There were too many students still inside the chamber.","If he created even a miniature sun here, the resulting explosion would not only kill Marbas. It could kill the unconscious students as well.","That was not a risk he was willing to take.","Noah slowly pushed himself back to his feet. Pain spread throughout his entire body. His ribs hurt. His muscles ached.","His mana reserves were also running low. Yet his blue eyes remained locked on Marbas.","The demon stood in the center of the ruined chamber. He was also wounded. Missing an arm. Covered in cuts and burns.","Yet still standing. Still stronger than all of them. Noah tightened his grip around his spear.","’We have no choice.’ He thought gravely.","’No matter what happens... we have to keep fighting.’","Nearby, Damien also stood up. For a brief moment, their eyes met.","Ocean blue eyes met hazel eyes.","No words were needed. Both of them understood exactly what the other was thinking.","The fight wasn’t over. And now they need to go all out no matter what would be the conclusion of this battle.","Golden light suddenly began to shine from Damien’s body. The glow spread across his skin and clothes.","His wounds slowly started healing. The cuts on his body closed little by little. His eyes turned completely golden.","Light mana surged through every part of his body. Unlike before, normal mana was no longer circulating inside him.","Only light remained. Heat radiated from him as if a star had awakened inside his chest.His special ability had activated.","Solar Core.","The temperature around him rose slightly.","Noah quickly reached into his storage pouch. He pulled out a healing potion and a mana recovery potion.","Without hesitation, he drank both. The familiar warmth spread through his body.","It wasn’t enough to fully restore him. But it would keep him fighting.","Marbas noticed Damien immediately.","His violet eyes narrowed. For the first time since the battle began, his expression became serious.","The golden light surrounding Damien felt wrong.","It was unnatural. It felt very dangerous and uncomfortable.","Even to a demon like him.","\"What are you, boy?\" Marbas asked curiously. The energy radiating from him was just too mysterious for the demon.","But before Damien could answer. A shadow moved behind Marbas.","There was no sound of footsteps.","Nor there was any warning.","Yet Marbas still sensed it. Or more like his instinct told him.","He instantly turned around.","A dagger coated in pure darkness slashed toward his neck.","The attacker was Kaelan. The one who was laying down before,but now standing once again. His hair were messy when gray eyes were calm and cold.","Marbas reacted immediately. His remaining fist shot forward. Dark violet mana covered his arm.","BOOM!","The fist collided with Kaelan’s dagger.","A powerful shockwave exploded outward. Cracks spread across the nearby floor.","However, something unusual happened.The dark violet mana coating Marbas’s fist began disappearing.","It flowed into Kaelan’s body.","It was being absorbed.","Marbas frowned after watching it. His attack had become weaker.","Kaelan’s ability, Black Star, allowed him to absorb mana from incoming attacks and reduce their power.","Unfortunately, the ability had limits. He could not use it constantly. Nor could he absorb too much mana at once.","Even after weakening the attack, the impact was still enormous.","\"Argh!\"","Kaelan was thrown backward. His body crashed across the stone floor. Blood appeared at the corner of his mouth.","Still, he forced himself back up. His breathing was rough. His body trembled from the damage.","Marbas looked at him. \"You got up again, young man. Why are you trying so hard..\"","The demon’s voice was calm.","\"Do you really think it will change anything?\"","Suddenly, a flash of golden light shot toward him.","Damien had attacked when Marbas hot distracted by Kaelan.","Two large magic circles appeared behind him. They glow with same golden light.","The first circle released a giant lance made entirely of light.","The second fired a concentrated beam of golden energy.","At the same time, Damien rushed forward with his sword.","Marbas snorted while watching him coming. Dark violet energy exploded from his body. Unlike most demons, Marbas relied heavily on martial combat.","His fists were his weapons. His body was his weapon. He dashed toward Damien.","Golden light and violet energy collided.","BOOM!","Marbas avoided the incoming spells with incredible speed. The lance and beam crashed into the floor behind him.","Massive explosions followed.","Stone shattered. Dust filled the air.","Meanwhile, Mary was moving around the battlefield. She carefully dragged unconscious students away from the fighting area.","Her eyes were worried while watching them.","She was in good condition compare to others, but not strong enough to fight...so she helped other in whichever way she could do.","CLANG!","BOOM!","Damien’s sword collided with Marbas’s fist.","Shockwaves spread through the chamber.","Marbas smiled slightly. \"You’ve become stronger, boy. Is that some kind of ability?\"","Damien didn’t reply. His focus remained completely on the battle.","He waited.Then he found an opening.","His leg shot forward.","BAM!","The kick landed directly on Marbas’s ribs. For the first time in several moments, the demon was forced backward.","He slid several meters across the floor.","Boah was waiting for this moment.","So at the same moment, Noah arrived. Cold mana erupted around him.","Eight ice weapons appeared in the air.","They were two spears, two swords, two axes and two arrows. All of them floated around Noah.","His face was pale. His eyes were bloodshot. A vein bulged on his forehead. Throbbing violently as if it would burst open at any moment.","He was forcing his Ice Creation ability beyond its normal limits.","The strain was immense.","Still, he didn’t stop.","Thkse weapon had appeared around Marbus in all directions.","With a snap of his fingers, all eight weapons launched forward.","They attacked from every direction.","Some attacked from above. Few move in down side.","Left and right side of demon.","Every angle was covered.","Marbas clicked his tongue.","\"No chance.\"","His remaining arm moved rapidly.","Punch.","Deflect.","Punch.","Deflect.","Several ice weapons shattered. But before he could fully recover.","Noah slammed his spear against the floor.","CRACK!","A thin layer of ice spread across the ground.","It moved quickly. Reaching Marbas in an instant. The floor beneath the demon froze solid."]},{"number":154,"title":"Chapter 154: One Chance","paragraphs":["Marbas’s footing slipped. His movement slowed for just a fraction of a second.","That tiny opening was enough. Two ice weapons struck him.","One hit his side.","The other cut across his shoulder.","Blood appeared.","\"Aregh!!\" He screamed in pain but instantly focused on battle.","Marbas’s eyes narrowed.","Then Damien moved. Golden light gathered around his sword. More and more mana poured into the blade. The weapon began shining like a piece of the sun itself.","Damien raised the sword high above his head.","His expression remained calm.","He was focused. And determined than ever.","Then he swung.","[Radiant Severance]","A massive golden arc exploded from the blade. The attack rushed forward with enough power to split the battlefield apart.","The air screamed around it. Everything in its path was illuminated by golden light.","At the same time, Noah thrust his spear into the floor.","Walls of ice erupted upward.","Total three ice walls erupted from the floor around the demon.","They surrounded Marbas from multiple sides. Only one path remained open.","The path directly facing Damien’s attack.","Marbas was trapped. This time a surprise appeared on his face. The golden slash rushed closer.","Its killing intent was unmistakable.","Marbas inhaled deeply. Dark violet energy exploded from his body. The chamber shook.","The ice walls around him cracked. The floor beneath him shattered. Then he lowered his stance.","One foot forward. One foot back. His remaining fist pulled behind him.","All of his power gathered into that single arm.","The violet energy compressed.","It was condensed. And became terrifyingly dense. Then Marbas punched. A gigantic dark violet fist of energy burst forward from his strike.","The attack surged toward Damien’s golden slash.","The two powers met in the center of the battlefield.","The Golden light and dark violet energy. For a single moment, everything became silent.","Then–","BOOOOOOM!!!","The collision exploded. A blinding flash swallowed the entire chamber.","This send Damien backward by the shockwaves.","The collision shook the entire chamber.","A violent storm of golden and violet energy swept outward, tearing apart the already damaged floor and walls. Dust, stone fragments, and shattered ice filled the air, reducing visibility to almost nothing.","Most people would have been blown away.","Noah wasn’t. The moment he saw the explosion coming, he thrust his spear into the ground and gripped it with both hands.","The force slammed into him. His feet slid backward several meters. Pain shot through his arms.","His muscles screamed. But he refused to let go. If he was blown away now, they would lose the pressure they had fought so hard to maintain.","So he endured. The shockwave gradually weakened. Dust continued to swirl throughout the chamber.","The air was thick with smoke and mana residue.","Noah pulled his spear free from the ground.","Then he moved.","Without hesitation and rest.","His body was reaching its limit. Every breath felt heavy. His lungs burned. His ribs ached from earlier injuries and taking so many shockwaves and impact of explosions.","Several muscles felt as though they might tear apart if he pushed any harder.","But none of that mattered, not right now.","’Move.’ The thought echoed inside his head.","’Keep moving.’ If they wanted to win, they couldn’t allow Marbas even a single moment to recover.","The demon was simply too powerful. Every second they gave him was another second for him to regain control of the battle.","They had to keep attacking. Keep pressuring him. Keep forcing him to defend.","Only then would they have a chance.","A tiny chance. But a chance nonetheless.","Noah ran forward through the dust cloud. His grip tightened around his spear. The smoke slowly began to clear. The ruined battlefield came into view.","Frozen patches of ice. Shattered floor.","And standing in the center of it all was Marbas.","The Demon who was behind all over this mess.","The demon was still alive. His breathing was noticeably heavier now. His clothes were in ruins.","Burns, cuts, and frost marks covered his body. The arm Damien had severed was still gone.","Fresh blood dripped from several wounds.Yet he remained standing.","Noah’s jaw clenched.","’Dammit.’","Even after everything. Even after all of their attacks. The demon was still standing.","But something had changed.","Marbas looked tired. First time since the battle began, Noah could clearly see it. The demon’s chest rose and fell more heavily.","The violet energy surrounding him had become thinner. His movements were no longer as effortles as before.","He was exhausted too.","Noah’s eyes sharpened. This was the closest they had ever come. The closest they had been to bringing down the demon.","Cold mana gathered around Noah’s spear. A thin layer of ice formed across the weapon.","The frost slowly spread along the shaft and blade. His mana reserves had partially recovered from the potion.","Around him, the sounds of battle faded from his awareness.","He could hear his own heartbeat.","Thump.","Thump.","Thump.","Across the battlefield, Marbas raised his head.","Their eyes met.","For a brief moment, neither moved. Predator and prey. Hunter and hunted.","Neither side knew which was which anymore.","Noah tightened his grip. The ice coating around his spear thickened. Cracks of frost spread beneath his feet.","’This is it.’","His blue eyes narrowed.","’This is my chance.’","Every remaining drop of mana inside his body surged toward the spear.","The cold around him intensified. White mist escaped from his mouth.","His muscles tensed. Ready to explode forward.","One attack and one opportunity. One strike that could decide everything. Then Noah kicked off the shattered floor and shot toward Marbas like an arrow released from a bow.","Meanwhile Lyria who was unconscious, now she was conscious.","It was because of explosion.","She saw Noah kovinv toward Marbas. But she notice that Noah, his breathing slowed.","He was really tired.","So she decided to help him. Her hand extended in Noah’s direction.","A magice circle suddenly appeared beneath Noah’s figure.","From it warm light covered his body, making him stronger and giving him a small boost."]},{"number":155,"title":"Chapter 155: The Last Chance","paragraphs":["Noah felt the change move through his body like a wave.","The aching in his muscles didn’t disappear entirely, the heaviness in his limbs lightened.","His breathing steadied, and the strength that had been draining out of him through the fight started returning in a slow but steady flow.","His stamina was coming back.","He knew exactly who had done it.","’It was done by Lyria. thanks’","He didn’t look back to confirm it. He just took what she had given him and used it.","He kicked off the ground.","The distance between him and Marbas closed in seconds, Noah driving forward with everything the boost had returned to him, spear leveled and ice already forming along the shaft.","Marbas saw him coming.","His smile widened despite the blood and the damage and the missing arm. Despite all of it, that dangerous composure he had was still there on his face.","\"You think you can kill me?\" His voice was heavy, the exhaustion in it undeniable now.","\"Dream on, boy.\" He was not bothered by Noah.","He raised his remaining arm to intercept.","And then stopped.","Not just slowed down, but it stopped completely, all at once, like something had reached inside him and simply removed his ability to move.","His eyes went glassy and unfocused, the outstretched arm frozen halfway through its motion.","He stood there rigid and unresponsive, staring at nothing.","Noah registered it in half a second and didn’t waste the other half asking questions.","He sent the command downward.","Ice erupted from the floor beneath Marbas’s feet, surging up around his ankles and calves and locking him in place.","A second layer of immobility over whatever had already taken hold of him.","Then Noah drove the spear forward.","The tip punched through Marbas’s chest with a wet, tearing sound that echoed across the chamber walls.","The daze state of the demon broke.","\"ARRGGH—!!\"","Marbas came back to himself in an instant. The scream ripping out of him as his eyes refocused and found Noah’s face directly in front of his own.","Blood welled up immediately around the spear shaft and ran down the blade in dark rivulets, dripping to the stone floor.","Noah didn’t pull back.","He twisted the spear.","Ice detonated from inside the wound. Sharp internal spikes bursting outward through the surrounding flesh with a sound that was considerably worse than the impact had been.","Marbas’s body shuddered violently against the restraints of the ice at his feet, another scream tearing out of him, raw and broken.","Noah held the spear in place and looked at him.","Across the chamber, people were moving.","Lyria had finished channeling the boost toward Noah. And immediately turned to the students around her. Moving between them with quick hands and calm efficiency. c","Checking pulses, helping people sit up, calling out to the ones who were still trying to find their footing.","Arisha was already on her feet.","Emma beside her, gauntlets still on, shaking the fog of the earlier fight out of her head with short sharp blinks.","Damien had gotten himself upright, one hand braced on his knee, sword still in his grip out of pure stubbornness.","On the far side of the chamber, Mary had disappeared from the main group and was moving along the stone wall in long quick strides.","Her hands pressing against the surface as she went, searching.","Noah pulled back slightly and looked at Marbas.","The demon was still standing. Barely... held upright as much by the ice around his legs as by anything in his own body.","His head had dropped forward. His breathing came in shallow, wet pulls. The blood from the wound was running freely now, pooling around the ice at his feet.","Then he coughed.","It was a broken voice. Filled with pain. Blood came with it, running down his chin and dripping from his jaw.","His inside were burning in pain at the same time the cold ice was there. Which he didn’t know whether it was soothing or pain or just intensifying it.","He raised his head slowly and looked up at Noah and smiled.","Marbas was not done yet. He still ha will to continue.","The smile he just show was the worst kind of smile.","The kind worn by someone who has already accepted something the other person hasn’t realized yet.","\"You did it,\" he said, his voice barely above a rasp. \"You are actually killing me.\"","Noah had seen this before.","The specific shape of this moment, someone dying with a smile on their face, telling you that you had won.","He had seen it. The man who had attacked inside the academy, controlling Patrick’s body, wearing that same expression at the end.","This gaves him same kind of feeling.","It had meant something then too. His grip on the spear tightened.","\"But...\" Marbas exhaled slowly, the smile not going anywhere. \"You’re too late.\"","His words only made Noah more tense.","Noah’s eyes moved past him.","Toward the wall. Where the carved eye sitting enormous and dominant across the entire back surface of the chamber.","The one he had been not thinking too hard about since they arrived.","His stomach dropped.","’The ritual. The entire point of bringing everyone here was the ritual. To sacrifice us!!’ He thought with pale expression.","\"Shittt—\"","He grabbed the spear shaft and pulled.","Marbas moved as well.","Despite everything, the spear through his chest, the ice holding his legs, the blood loss.","He still moved. One arm came up and the hand closed around Noah’s wrist in a grip that had no business being as strong as it was.","The spear tore further inside him as he lurched forward. He didn’t seem to notice or care.","\"You can’t run away,\" Marbas said quietly.","Then Mary’s voice rang from across the hall.","\"EVERYONE!! THERE’S A DOOR OVER HERE!! COME NOW!!\"","Noah’s head snapped toward the sound.","Mary, she was standing at the far wall, pressed against a section of stone that looked identical to every other section of stone around it."]},{"number":156,"title":"Chapter 156: Another Unknown Being","paragraphs":["Mary, she had found a door.","How she had found it and how she had gotten it open, Noah had no idea, but it was open and it led somewhere that wasn’t here.","He filled his lungs with air.","\"EVERYONE!! GET OUT OF HERE RIGHT NOW!!\"","His voice hit every corner of the chamber and came back from the walls. Students who had been mid-movement froze for a second and then moved faster.","Damien’s head came up and his eyes found Noah across the space. worry there, sharp and immediate.","\"DON’T WORRY ABOUT ME!!\" Noah held his gaze.","\"DAMIEN, TAKE EVERYONE OUT!!\"","Damien’s jaw worked.","Then he gritted his teeth and turned.","Grabbing the nearest student by the arm and pulling them toward Mary’s door.","Lyria was already moving, one arm supporting a student who couldn’t walk unassisted. Steering him firmly in the right direction.","Arisha cast one last look toward Noah.","Her golden eyes finding him across the chaos, reading his face for a second. Then made a decision.","She got her shoulder under another student who was struggling and broke into a run.","The hall filled with the sound of footsteps and people calling out to each other, everyone moving in the direction at the door in the wall.","Few of them still remained behind.","But when life on line, they could help everyone.","So, they help as many as possible.","But few still remained behind.","While Marbas started laughing.","It was a ruined sound, broken by blood and damage. But it carried through the chamber clearly enough.","\"HAHAHAHA!!\" His voice rose, raw and unhinged, echoing off the stone.","\"NO ONE GETS AWAY FROM THIS!! I — MARBAS ACHERON! SACRIFICE MYSELF TO YOU, MY LORD!! ACCEPT MY OFFERING!! ACCEPT THESE LIVES AND MY OWN FOR YOUR GLORY!!\"","The symbols appeared on his skin.","Dark red markings erupted across every surface of Marbas’s body. His skin, then his face, his remaining arm. They started to glow.","From beneath like something burning inside him was leaking out through every crack.","The same symbols spread outward from him to the floor and then climbed the walls and found the enormous carved eye at the back of the chamber.","The eye began to glow.","The same dark red, deep and pulsing, the vertical pupil filling with light from its edges inward.","\"DAMMIT—\"","Noah didn’t think.","His free hand snapped up and an ice dagger formed in his palm in under a second.","It was small and sharp.","It conjured from nothing but urgency and whatever mana he had left.","He drove it down across Marbas’s wrist.","The grip didn’t release immediately.","He slashed again, harder, and the second cut found something vital enough that the fingers spasmed and loosened.","Noah ripped his arm free and stumbled back few steps back.","He looked at the wall.","The eye was still glowing. The symbols on Marbas’s body were burning brighter.","Noah turned and ran.","His boots hit the stone floor in hard rapid impacts.","Each stride pushing everything his body had left into the next one.","The door was visible ahead.","The gap in the wall where Mary had forced it open, a sliver of dim light coming through from the other side.","Most of his group were already through it.","He could see the few students ahead of him scrambling toward the opening.","While there were few behind him.","Some running, some half-limping, some pulling each other forward by the arm.","Noah couldn’t help anyone who was behind him.","Afterall his own life was on line.","Behind him, Marbas was still laughing.","The sound of it had changed.","It wasn’t the controlled, composed voice of a demon who had been managing the situation perfectly.","It was something looser than that.","Something that had let go of all pretense and was just laughing because nothing mattered to it anymore.","Noah didn’t look back.","He heard it anyway.","The deep resonant pulse that came from the wall.","It was not a sound exactly, more like pressure moving through the stone and the air and the floor beneath his feet simultaneously.","The torches along the walls flickered and then extinguished one by one in rapid sequence as something consumed the light around them.","He looked back once.","He couldn’t help it.","The carved eye on the wall was gone.","In its place was a portal. It was enormous, consuming the entire back wall of the chamber from floor to ceiling.","Its surface a churning deep black that moved like liquid but wasn’t liquid, like darkness given depth and dimension and looked like there was another world on that sude of darkness.","The red glow that had preceded it pulsed from somewhere within, coloring the edges of the portal in dark crimson.","Then something came through it.","It emerged slowly, which was somehow worse than if it had come fast.","A shape pushing through the black surface of the portal the way something large pushes through water.","\"It moved slowly and heavily, with no rush at all, as if nothing in the room could make it hurry.","A skull.","Massive. Goat-shaped. The bone surface was yellowed and ancient, deep scratches and fractures running across it like a record of things it had survived. Two enormous curved horns rose from the top of the cranium and swept outward and upward, each one longer than a grown man was tall. The jaw hung slightly open and the teeth within it were countless and uneven, packed together in rows that had no concern for symmetry or function beyond the obvious one.","And in the eye sockets — set deep within the bone — two points of dark red light burned like coals that had never gone cold.","They moved.","They found the room. They swept across it with the slow patience of something that had waited a very long time and was in no rush now that it had arrived.","Noah faced forward and pushed harder.","The door was close. Twenty meters. Fifteen.","Behind him Marbas screamed.","But not in pain this time.","But in ecstasy, the voice of a man watching the exact thing he had devoted everything to finally happen in front of him.","\"YES!! ACCEPT MY OFFERING MY LORD!! TAKE THEM!! TAKE—\"","The jaw came down.","It closed with a loud sound. It was dangerous.","It was a killing force.","A powerful wave of wind and some kind of dark energy burst outward from the point of impact.","And moved forward to hit everything in the chamber at once."]},{"number":157,"title":"Chapter 157: Finally Safe","paragraphs":["The shockwave came out of the skull’s mouth like the world itself had decided to exhale.","It moved through the chamber in every direction at once, and the first thing it found was Marbas.","His body didn’t fall. It simply came apart in flesh and bone. And everything that had made up the demon Marbas, reducing itself to particles in a single instant.","It was brutal yet efficient.","The particles becoming mist, the mist becoming blood that hung in the air for a while before dropping to the stone floor.","There was no scream. There was no final expression. One moment he existed and then he simply didn’t. The shockwave kept moving.","The students who had fallen behind reached its edge one by one.","Noah heard them.","He didn’t turn around. He made a decision not to turn around and kept running forward. But he heard each one. He heard a sound coming from behind.","There was a wet, percussive sound. It was repeating itself down the line of running footsteps behind him.","The sounds were not something he would forget quickly.","He kept running.","’I need to run!’ He said.","He knew that those students behind him, they were getting killed on by one. The door was right there. He lunged forward and hit the frame.","He threw himself through the gap, tumbling out the other side.","Then he hit the ground hard, rolling once before stopping face down on the stone floor.","He lay still for a second.","His lungs were working. His hands were on the ground. He came through that door.","From behind the door, the red light pulsed.","That red lightly mostly because of the blood.","Noah glanced behind.","There slow and deep red liquid moving through the stone. And painting the floor.","He watched it just for few seconds. And everything clicked to him, what might happened.","He could feel something was coming toward him.","He trued to get up.","Just then.","Hands grabbed his collar.","\"NOAH!!\"","It was Mary who grab him. Her grip was tight and urgent, pulling him upright with more strength than he would have credited her.","\"I’m here,\" she said. His voice came out rough and urgeng. \"I was waiting for you here.\"","She said. Her short black hairs end sticking to her skin with sweat.","Her expression worried and with fear.","\"We need to move.\" Her face was pale behind the round glasses but her eyes were steady. \"Right now...we need to move.\"","He got his feet under him and looked back at the door.","The red glow from the chamber came through the gap in another slow pulse. Stronger than the one before it.","\"Close it,\" he said.","\"Can’t lock it from this side...I don’t know..\" she said hurriedly.","The pulse came again. The stone under his feet vibrated faintly with it.","Noah grabbed Mary’s arm.","\"Then we run as fast as we can.\"","They started to run.","The tunnel ahead was rough cave rock on all sides, dark except for the light coming from the exit visible ahead.","A pale natural opening maybe fifty meters away where the tunnel met open air.","The sound of their boots on stone filled the passage as Noah and Mary pushed toward it.","Few students still running forward.","Then something came through the door behind them.","It was not the skull. It was the same force of it. The force past through the door.","A pressure wave moving through the tunnel like a fist through a corridor.","Hitting the walls and the ceiling and compressing down the passage at speed.","The whole tunnel shook, loose stone dropping from the ceiling in fragments.","Noah registered it coming and didn’t think.","He stepped in front of Mary, grabbed her, and pulled her into his arms.","Turning his back to what was behind them, putting himself between her and it.","Mary’s black eyes went wide. \"Noah!!! what are you—\"","He lifted her and ran faster.","\"Protecting you,\" he said. \"I think.\"","\"Why—\"","The wall of ice he had thrown up across his back shattered.","Something hit him.","\"ARRGHHH—!!\"","The force drove him forward off his feet entirely.","Both of them launched through the air, covering the last stretch of tunnel in a way that had nothing to do with running.","His back felt like it had been opened. His coat was gone, shredded away, and the skin beneath it was shredded too.","He couldn’t tell exactly what the damage was.","The pain was too large and too general to read specific details from it. Blood hit the air behind them in a spray.","His skin on back was tear apart. As if it was peeled by someone. All remained was bloodied back.","They came out of the tunnel exit.","The open air and the green of the forest hit Noah’s face as they tumbled out into it.","The light sudden and sharp after the darkness of the tunnel.","Mary came out of his arms and rolled across the grass and into a low bush at the side of the clearing.","Noah hit a tree trunk back-first and bounced off it and went down face forward into the dirt and roots at its base.","He lay there.","He could hear the forest. Birds somewhere above. Wind in the canopy.","Completely ordinary sounds existing alongside the fact that he was bleeding heavily from his back and couldn’t currently feel his legs properly.","The evening orange light pass through the canopy of trees.","He turned his head to the side.","Other students were scattered around the clearing.","The ones who had made it through ahead of him, who had come out further from the exit and taken less of what he had absorbed directly.","They were down too, some unconscious, some groaning quietly. Injured and some more admaged. But breathing alive.","Less damage than him. Considerably less.","Damien, Arisha, Kaelan and others lay the.","He looked back toward where the tunnel exit had been.","There were just trees.","Green and ordinary and completely calm.","As though the cave and the tunnel and the chamber with the carved eye had never existed here before.","The rock face was gone. The opening was gone. The darkness inside was gone.","Whatever that place had been, it had taken itself away."]},{"number":158,"title":"Chapter 158: A New Reward Soon","paragraphs":["Noah stared at the trees for a moment.","Then his eyes started getting heavy.","The blood was still running from his back. He could feel it moving warm and continuous.","Which was not a good sign.","His hands were shaking where they pressed into the dirt.","The pain had been enormous a moment ago and was now starting to become strangely distant, which was also not a good sign.","He thought about Mary.","He hadn’t made a plan to protect her. He hadn’t thought it through.","He had just done it.","His body had moved on instinct.","Maybe because she had been there through all of it.","Maybe because he had already seen or say guess, what had happened to the ones who didn’t make it.","And he hadn’t been able to stop that...but he could stop this.","He thought about the students whose footsteps had stopped in the tunnel behind him.","He didn’t feel guilty.","He knew clearly and without self-deception.","That he couldn’t have saved them.","Running had been the only option.","Staying would have meant dying alongside them. That was not a choice he was willing to make and he wasn’t going to punish himself for it.","But he had still heard them. The sound of something wet...something exploding.","He would be hearing them for a while. His vision was narrowing at the edges.","’I survive....but...can I stay alive.’ He thought.","He wanted to pull out remaining healing potions and drank them.","But his back was too injured.","Then the screen appeared.","It materialized in front of his face the same way it always did.","It was clean and clear, completely indifferent to the blood and the dirt and the fact that he was lying broken against a tree root.","[A reward is available. Would you like to claim it? ]","[ YES ]","He had seen this before. After the dungeon with Damien. After killing that creature.","This same screen had appeared immediately and he had kept it like that without claiming the reward. There had been no urgency then.","There was urgency now.","The blood loss was real.","The darkness coming in from the edges of his vision was real.","He was loosing consciousness.","He was a long way from the forest edge and he had no idea how long before Morgana or anyone else found them.","The fear was simple and honest to him.","’What if I die out here before anyone reaches me.’","He moved his right hand.","It took more effort than it should have. His arm was shaking and slick with blood.","And dragging it across the ground to bring his index finger in line with the glowing YES on the screen.","It felt like moving something that had forgotten it belonged to him.","He got there.","His finger touched it.","[ YES ]","He clicked.","---","The forest around them had stopped looking like a forest.","What had been dense woodland twenty minutes ago was now a landscape of craters and scorched earth and fallen trees.","The ground torn open in multiple places and the canopy above shredded down to bare.","But that was what happened when two people at that level decided the same stretch of forest was where they were going to fight.","Morgana came in low with the black spear and released the darkness mana through it in a concentrated burst that hit the groun.","Where Buer had been standing and tore a trench three meters deep through the earth. He was already above her.","Having pushed off a half-destroyed tree trunk to clear the attack, both swords coming down.","She rolled sideways and the blades hit stone instead of her.","The aura on them detonating against the rock and throwing shrapnel in every direction.","She was back on her feet before the debris settled.","Buer landed and turned to face her.","They stood across from each other in the ruined clearing.","Both of them breathing harder than when this had started.","His cracked sword had finally given out sometime in the last exchange.","The blade had split fully and he had discarded the pieces.","Fighting with one sword now. Burns and cuts distributed across his chest and arms.","The damaged shoulder from her earlier spell was still affecting his range.","Morgana’s hand was still bleeding. There was a cut along her jaw from debris she hadn’t moved fast enough to avoid.","Her hair was completely loose, falling around her face, the neat bun from earlier a distant memory.","She raised the black spear.","Buer didn’t raise his sword.","He lowered it. Until the tip pointed at the ground.","Morgana’s eyes narrowed.","He looked at her for a moment, and then the expression on his face shifted into something that wasn’t a smile.","Like a man who had just received news or notice somethinb that was both good and bad at the same time.","\"It seems we only managed halfway,\" he said.","Morgana said nothing. She kept the spear up.","Buer tilted his head slightly. \"You want to know where your students ended up, don’t you?\" He glanced at her coat pocket.","\"You have something that tracks them. I know you do.... your type always does.\" He took one step back, his sword arm dropping fully to his side. \"Check it. Go on...go save your students.\"","She watched him for two full seconds.","Then she reached into her coat and pulled out the tracking device with her free hand, never dropping the spear, never fully taking her eyes off him.","She clicked it on.","The projection populated above the surface.","The missing signals were back.","Not all of them... a handful of markers that had been absent since they first disappeared were still gone.","Which sent a cold blade of dread through her chest that she didn’t let reach her face.","But the majority of them were there, clustered in a location deep in the forest.","Far from the cave area and far from where they should have been.","They were alive. Most of them alive.","The relief that moved through her was involuntary and she didn’t try to stop it.","She raised her eyes from the device.","Buer was gone.","No displaced air.","Just the empty ruined clearing in front of her, the broken trees.","She stood there for exactly one second.","Her jaw tightened.","She had questions for him,","She put the device away and turned.","The direction the tracker had shown was east and deep.","She oriented on it and pushed mana into her legs. More than she had been using during the fight, the reserves she had been managing carefully now given a different purpose entirely.","She moved.","The broken forest blurred past her on both sides.","Her expression was set and cold and entirely focused.","Her students were out there.","Everything else could wait."]},{"number":159,"title":"Chapter 159: Monarch Of The Frost","paragraphs":["Darkness surrounded Noah.","He could no longer feel the forest.","He could no longer hear the wind, the voices of the surviving students, or the pain tearing through his body.","Everything felt distant.","It was fading","As if he were slowly sinking into a deep ocean where neither light nor sound could reach him.","Then the familiar blue screen appeared before him once more.","Its light floated within the darkness. Words began appearing across its surface. He somehow tried to focus on it.","---","[Congratulations, Extra!]","[For successfully surviving the Third Act of Chapter I – Demons.]","[Not only did you survive an encounter against a demon, but you also came into contact with something that was never supposed to appear at this stage, in this arc.]","[You witnessed a fragment, or say a weakest form of The Eternal Mona@#$ of the S@#$%#$#@, @$%#@#$.]","The text glitched violently. Several words distorted beyond recognition.","Noah couldn’t understand any of it. The symbols looked wrong.","Not unreadable. They were wrong. For some reason he couldn’t see them. His heavy eyes blinked.","As if his mind simply wasn’t meant to process them. The system continued regardless.","[As a reward, you will receive—]","The message suddenly stopped. Several seconds passed.","[Wait!! What are you doing here?]","Noah blinked weakly. The system was talking in slight tense tone. The line looked panicked.","[Damn! What do you mean, what am I doing here?]","Then a completely different line appeared. Another voice came, that wasn’t the system. The mechanical tone was gone.","The voice sounded offended. A new voice appeared. It was a male voice. As if someone had just asked him an extremely stupid question.","It was loud and confident. And it had emotions, unlike the emotionless system.","[I felt something from that place you’re connected to just now!]","[It was very weak, but someone as amazing as me can sense things from very far away! I can see that thing already left...but I can sense its traces.]","[Hahaha! I really am amazing!]","The male voice said while laughing.","Noah stared blankly. He had no idea what was happening anymore.","The system seemed just as confused.","[Wait! I still need to reward the Extra!]","The mechanical voice spoke again. The male voice immediately responded.","[Oh?You mean that boy?Noah?Let me take a look at him—]","A brief pause followed. Then the man’s voice exploded.","[THE HELL?! HE’S DYING, YOU IDIOT BITCH!]","Noah felt strangely offended despite barely being conscious.","The system sounded annoyed.","[Oh, come on. He won’t die. Help is already on the way. According to calculations, his survival rate remains acceptable.]","The man’s reaction was immediate.","[Tch!]","He clicked his tongue.","[This is exactly why I hate systems! Always calculating everything.]","[Always acting smart. Those system genre novels are no fun because of this. Getting stronger on your own. Without help, that kind of novels are better.]","Noah had absolutely no idea who this person was. But somehow he sounded more alive than the system ever had.","The man continued.","[Forget that. This kid just survived THAT thing. Do you have any idea how insane that is?]","[He deserves something good.]","The system immediately panicked. For the first time since Noah had obtained it, he could actually sense panic in its voice.","[Wait!]","[No! Do not do that!]","The man sounded confused.","[Why not?]","[Because it is too early!]","[Far too early! That reward is not meant to be given at this point!]","The man went silent. Then he laughed.","[Hahaha!]","[And?]","The system almost sounded desperate now.","[It will heavily affect future developments! The timeline will shift! Multiple projected paths will become unstable!]","The man didn’t seem concerned Not even slightly.","[Hmm. Sounds like a future problem.]","[It Is a future problem!]","[Not my future.]","The system fell silent.","Noah would have laughed if he wasn’t busy dying. The man spoke again. This time his voice carried excitement.","[Besides, we’re not giving him the full thing.]","[We’re only helping him awaken it.]","[And honestly?]","[He’s the perfect candidate.]","[NO!]","The system practically screamed.","[DO NOT—]","The man interrupted.","[Too late.]","A strange warmth spread through the darkness.","Noah couldn’t see anything. Yet somehow he felt something changing. Something deep inside him.","Something ancient. Something sleeping.","The man’s voice echoed one final time.","[Take this, Noah Eldritch.]","The blue screen flashed. New words appeared.","[Reward Obtained]","[Bloodline Acquired]","[Monarch of Frost]","The moment the words appeared. Everything changed. A terrible cold spread throughout Noah’s body.","At first it felt refreshing. Then it was uncomfortable.","Then it was painful, then horrifying.","The cold wasn’t covering his skin.","It wasn’t outside him. It was inside him. His blood began freezing. His veins turned icy. His heartbeat slowed.","It was getting slower by each second.","The freezing sensation spread deeper. Into his muscles. Into his organs. Into his bones. Into every single cell of his body.","It felt as if winter itself had entered him and claimed ownership over his existence. Far away, the system watched.","Or perhaps whatever space existed beyond reality watched. The mechanical voice sounded horrified.","[You actually did it!!]","The man sounded surprisingly calm.","[Of course I did.]","[You forcibly awakened the bloodline! His body cannot handle this!]","[Tch!]","The man clicked his tongue once again.","[You’re such a useless system.]","The man sighed dramatically.","[You systems are supposed to help transmigrators become stronger. Instead you spend half your time worrying about rules.]","---","Noah’s body continued freezing. The process showed no signs of stopping. His blood became ice. His organs became ice.","His heart became ice.His body temperature dropped beyond what should have been possible.","Then his skin turned pale blue.","Moments later, his entire body froze.","It was completely frozen. From the outside, Noah now looked like a perfect ice sculpture.","Not a single movement remained. Not a single heartbeat. Not even a single breath.","Silence filled the space. The system spoke again.","[He’s dead.]","The man snorted.","[No, he’s not.]","[There are no signs of life.]","[That’s because you’re looking at it wrong.]","The system remained silent.","The man sighed.","[Honestly, who designed you?]","Several seconds passed.","Then the man suddenly laughed.","[Actually, never mind.I know exactly who designed you. That bastard. Also relax. ]","The man sounded entirely unbothered.","[ This particular bloodline will never kill its bearer. Not once. That’s the whole point of it]","[You cannot know that he— ]","[I can and I do. Stop panicking. Let me handle it. I will help him]","The system immediately stopped responding.","Almost as if it didn’t want to continue that conversation. Then something appeared above Noah’s frozen body.","A tiny black droplet.","It was mall and dark. Completely ordinary in appearance.","Yet its existence felt wrong. As though reality itself disliked having it nearby.","The droplet slowly descended.","It touched the ice.","Crack.","A single fracture line appeared across the surface, running from the point of contact outward in both directions.","Then another crack branched off it. Then another.","The sound of it was quiet at first.","It was delicate, like the surface of a frozen puddle being pressed from beneath and then it built.","The fracture lines multiplying and spreading until the entire shell of ice covering Noah’s body was a web of connected breaks.","Then it shattered.","The pieces didn’t fly outward.","They simply fell. Dropping away from his body and hitting the ground around him before dissolving into water and then into nothing.","Leaving the grass and roots dry.","What was underneath the ice was Noah.","His back wounds still present, still serious.","But color returning to his skin and the slight but unmistakable movement of his chest as his lungs remembered what they were for.","His heart started beating again.","[He’s... he’s alright. ]","The system said it quietly, like it was still deciding whether to believe it.","[Obviously.]","The man’s voice carried the easy confidence of someone who had never seriously considered the alternative.","[ You thought I would awaken something in him that would kill him? What kind of being do you take me for? He was already compatible. His body just needed to be shown what was already inside it. ]","[ ...]","[ I know who told you that a strong body was required for this awakening.]","The man continued, something shifting in his tone.","It was still light, but with an edge underneath it now.","[And I know whose plan I’ve just disrupted by moving this early. He’s going to be furious with me.]","A pause.","[ ...Hehe. Once again I did it.]","[This is not something to laugh about.]","[ It is a little bit]","He sounded genuinely entertained by his own recklessness.","[ Anyway. I’m done here. It was more interesting than I expected]","The man said.","[ Wait– I still have questions about what you just did– ]","[Goodbye, Noah Eldritch]","The voice spoke directly now, the way it hadn’t quite done before.","It aimed specifically rather than general.","It was meant for the unconscious young man lying in the dirt rather than for the system it had been arguing with.","[ I don’t know your whole story yet. But you survived that ]","A brief pause.","[ I think you’ll survive the rest of it too...I hope so..]","Then the voice was gone.","The system said nothing for a moment.","[ ...]","Then it too went quiet, and the screen dissolved, and the forest clearing returned to its ordinary sounds.","Wind in the canopy above, birds that had come back to the branches.","The distant sound of someone moving through the trees at high speed toward the cluster of injured students lying in the grass.","Noah’s chest rose.","It fell and rose again.","His body was healed completely."]},{"number":160,"title":"Chapter 160: Thinking about the Events.","paragraphs":["Morgana reached the clearing and stopped.","Fifteen students scattered across the grass and roots and dirt.","Most of them flat on their backs or crumpled against the trees at the clearing’s edge.","Some were breathing visibly. Some were still enough that she had to look twice.","She moved immediately.","She went from student to student in quick succession, two fingers to each throat.","Checking pulses and breathing and the visible severity of injuries.","Her expression stayed controlled throughout.","Not because she wasn’t feeling anything but because falling apart in the next thirty seconds would help nobody.","Most were alive. Injured, some badly, but they were still alive.","She found Damien on one side of the clearing.","He was lumped against a root with his sword still somehow in his hand.","She checked him. His pulse were normal, breathing regular, cuts and bruising across his arms and torso but nothing immediately life threatening.","She exhaled through her nose and moved on.","She counted as she went. Thirteen students were found alive.","She didn’t let herself think yet about the ones who weren’t here.","The signals that hadn’t reappeared on the tracker.","She found Noah near the tree line.","He was face down, one arm extended, the back of his coat shredded away entirely.","The skin beneath it was normal and cleaned. His fair skin perfectly normal and healthy.","He was not injured.","For some reason that felt weird to her. His clothes were shredded that means he must have been attacked by something. Yet there was no injury.","She turned him carefully onto his side and checked his breathing. It was normal.","She looked at the body for any other injuries again.","She decided to put that thought aside and reached into her storage ring.","The communication device came out and she pressed the channel for the other instructors without hesitation.","\"Victor. Lucia. I need everyone at my location now.\" She read off the coordinates from the tracker.","\"Thirteen students down. Multiple serious injuries. Come prepared.\"","She didn’t wait for extended responses.","She clicked the channel closed and pulled out a small case from the same ring.","Healing potions, four of them. The concentrated that were not standard issue for field trips but that she had brought anyway because she always brought them anyway.","She started with the worst cases first.","Tipping a student’s head back carefully and getting the potion down took patience she currently had to construct one breath at a time.","The fourth potion she held for a moment, looking between two students.","By the time she heard footsteps crashing through the forest. Coming toward her.","She stood up and turned as Victor arrived first. Broad and fast for his size.","His expression already reading the scene before he fully entered the clearing.","Lucia came in from a different angle thirty seconds later with two of her own students who had been close to the forest edge and had medical training.","Atticus was last, and with him came three more instructors she didn’t immediately recognize.","Support staff from the academy group who had clearly been running since they got the call.","\"What happened?\" Victor asked, already crouching beside the nearest student.","\"I don’t have all of it yet,\" Morgana said.","\"Stabilize everyone first. Then we talk.\"","He looked at her for a moment.","At the cut along her jaw and the blood on her spear hand and the state of general dishevelment that was very unlike Morgana Celestine and then nodded and got to work without further questions.","It took another twenty minutes to get everyone stable, loaded onto emergency carry frames, and moving toward the city.","Morgana walked beside Damien’s frame and beside Noah’s and didn’t say anything to either of them.","They were unconscious. She said it anyway, quietly, in a tone that was less warm and more like a statement of non-negotiable fact.","\"You’re both fine.\"","Victor came and stand beside her. As the staff were taking away other students.","Morgana remained silent and then said in serious voice. \"There was a Demon in forest... I don’t think one...but multiple..\"","She continued to talk telling Morgana in detailed.","---","Noah opened his eyes to a white ceiling.","He stared at it for a moment without moving, trying to get the information available to him. White ceiling.","The smell of medicinal herbs.","It was clean and slightly sharp.","The particular scent of a place where warm healing magic had been used recently and often.","Soft ambient light from fixtures along the walls rather than windows.","Which meant it was either night or the room had no windows.","He turned his head.","It was night.","Through the single window at the far end of the large hall.","The sky was a deep dark blue with stars visible between clouds.","He was in a hospital.","Oakhaven City, it wasn’t the academy medical wing, the ceiling was too high and the hall too wide and the beds too numerous.","Large enough to have taken in the entire group of injured students, which it clearly had, because on the beds around him were familiar faces, most of them sleeping.","He sat up slowly.","His back pulled when he moved tight and tender.","He reached back and touched it carefully through the hospital shirt he was now wearing.","The wounds were closed. There was no shredded skin like before. He was perfectly healed.","He lay back down and looked at the ceiling again.","His mind went immediately to what it had been circling since the clearing.","The goat looking skull with huge curved horns.","The size of it.","The way it had come through the portal in the wall without hurrying, like it had all the time that existed and saw no reason to use less of it.","The red light in the eye sockets moving across the chamber.","The sound the jaw had made when it closed. That shockwave that had moved through stone and air and flesh with equal disregard for what it was passing through.","The students who hadn’t made it out.","He didn’t close his eyes against the thought. He let it sit where it was and looked at it plainly.","Then his mind moved to the conversation.","The system, who’s voice he had heard only three times before, and fourth time today.","the same mechanical voice...but there was one more voice that came beside it.","The man who was casual and loud. He was entirely unconcerned with whatever rules or plans or timelines which were apparently disrupted by showing up.","’Monarch of the Frost.’","Noah looked at the ceiling.","The bloodline was inside him now.","He couldn’t feel it clearly.","It was subtle, sitting somewhere beneath the surface of his awareness like something that had always been there and was simply now awake.","Cold in a way that wasn’t uncomfortable.","And one more thing...he felt stronger. His mana reserved looked increased.","He thought about the man’s last words.","’I think you’ll survive the rest of it too.’","He had no idea who that voice belonged to. He had no frame of reference for it.","The personality or the apparent ability to simply walk into a system space uninvited and start handing out rewards that weren’t on the approved list.","Which meant it was something that even system couldn’t go against.","He was not someone who was behind the system, someone who gave it to Noah. Rather he was someone else entirely.","Something outside that he could think about.","He exhaled slowly and let his eyes close.","Outside the window the night sky sat quiet and full of stars over Oakhaven City.","Completely indifferent to the fact that somewhere beneath it a goat skull the size of a building had briefly pushed its way into the world.","And then it gone back to wherever it had come from, for now at least.","Noah pulled the blanket up and decided that the rest of the thinking could wait until morning.","His back still hurt and he had survived something today that he was increasingly certain he wasn’t supposed to have survived.","And that was enough to process for one night."]},{"number":161,"title":"Chapter 161: Trying To Cheer Up Protagonist","paragraphs":["The morning sun had just begun rising above the city skyline.","Golden rays spilled across the rooftops and streets below, painting the city in warm colors.","Merchants were already opening their shops, and distant voices drifted upward from the bustling roads beneath.","Sitting on the chair near the large window of the recovery room, Noah stretched his arms above his head before letting out a long yawn.","\"Yawn~\"","His blue eyes lazily watched the city outside.","No life-threatening situations.","Just a normal morning.","\"Enjoying the morning view?\"","A familiar voice suddenly came from behind him.","Noah didn’t even need to turn around to know who it was.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"Yes...\" Noah replied while keeping his gaze outside. \"Can’t I do that?\"","Damien chuckled softly.","\"Yes, you can.\"","Noah finally turned around.","Damien was holding a chair in one hand. The young man looked far better than he had during the battle, though traces of exhaustion still lingered beneath his eyes.","Walking over, Damien placed the chair beside Noah’s and sat down.","For a few moments, neither of them spoke.","Both simply watched the city below.","The comfortable silence lasted only briefly before Noah glanced sideways.","\"You okay?\" he asked.","Damien’s expression remained calm as he nodded.","\"Yes, I am.\"","His answer came quickly.","Too quickly.","Noah raised an eyebrow.","The words said one thing.","The tone said another.","A faint sadness lingered beneath Damien’s voice.","It wasn’t obvious.","Most people probably wouldn’t notice it.","But Noah did.","After everything they had gone through together, it wasn’t difficult to guess what was bothering him.","Noah looked forward again.","His gaze drifted toward the busy streets outside.","\"Are you...\" he began slowly, \"thinking about those who died?\"","The question caused Damien’s expression to stiffen slightly.","His hands tightened together on his lap.For a moment, he didn’t answer.The silence itself was answer enough.","Noah wasn’t surprised.","After all, Damien was the protagonist.The hero. The kind of person who genuinely wanted to save others.","Someone who would gladly risk himself if it meant protecting people around him. But reality didn’t always care about good intentions.","Yesterday had proven that. They had run. They had survived. Yet not everyone had escaped.","Noah could still remember those disappearing footsteps behind him.","The memory wasn’t pleasant.","Damien lowered his head slightly. A bitter smile appeared on his face.","\"Hah...\"","He released a quiet breath.","\"I am happy to see that you survived.\" Noah said.","Damien’s eyes shifted toward Noah.","\"...but what about the others? Don’t you feel anything?\"","Noah remained silent for several seconds. His expression became thoughtful. Then he leaned back slightly in his chair.","\"Why?\"","Damien blinked.","Noah continued calmly.","\"It’s already a miracle that I survived.\"","His voice wasn’t cold.","It was simply honest.","\"It wasn’t something within my capabilities to help everyone.\"","His eyes moved toward the bright city outside.","\"I decided to put myself first and survive.\"","A small shrug followed.","\"There’s nothing wrong with that.\"","Damien listened quietly.","Noah folded his arms.","\"That’s the instinct of a living being.\"","His gaze remained fixed on the streets below.","\"Every creature in this world naturally puts its own life first.\"","The words came without hesitation.","Noah believed them completely. \"Everyone wants to survive.\"","A small smile appeared on his face.","Damien let out a weak laugh.","To be honest, Noah had no idead what words he need to use here. So he could cheer up the protagonist.","So he decided to use any line he remembered reading in novels.","Sadly they were broken...it’s not like he remembered those lines in detailed.","Noah continued to talk as he glanced at him. \"So don’t be sad.\"","His voice softened slightly. \"Be happy.\"","Damien looked at him.","Noah continued. \"Because of you, we managed to save fifteen students.\"","The number hung in the air between them.","Total fifteen.","Nine were dead.","The number was not enough but not insignificant either.","\"It would have been wrong if saving everyone had been possible and we simply chose not to.\"","His expression became serious.","\"But that situation wasn’t in our hands.\"","Images of the giant skull flashed through Noah’s mind.","The horrifying pulse. The students disappearing behind him. Marbas being erased as if he had never existed.","Even now, the memory made his stomach tighten.","No one could have stopped that.","Damien stared at the floor for a few moments.","Then he slowly nodded. \"I guess you’re right...But its not because of me..but because of us that more than half people survied. We all together survied and save each other.\"","A grin immediately appeared on Noah’s face.","\"Of course.\"","Damien rolled his eyes slightly.","Noah leaned forward and pointed at him. \"What you should do now is become stronger.\"","His tone became more determined.","\"So that in the future, when something like this happens again, you can help people instead of running for your life.\"","The words weren’t meant as criticism.","Only motivation.","Damien understood that. A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"Of course I will.\"","The sadness in his eyes seemed lighter than before.","It was not gone but it had became lighter.","Noah nodded in satisfaction. Then his expression softened. \"...and I believe you’re also happy that your friends survived.\"","Damien looked at him. This time his smile became genuine.","A warm smile.","\"Yes.\"","He nodded slowly.","\"I am.\"","His gaze moved toward the window.","Toward the city.","Toward the future.","\"I am happy that you and the others survived.\"","For a brief moment, neither of them spoke. The atmosphere felt lighter now.","It was less burdened.","The conversation had eased some of the guilt Damien had been carrying.","Eventually, Noah stretched his arms again and changed the topic.","\"So when are we going back?\"","He folded his arms behind his head.","\"Any idea?\"","Damien thought for a moment.","\"Hmm...\"","He looked outside as if estimating something.","\"Maybe in the evening.\"","\"Evening, huh...\"","Noah sighed dramatically. \"I really want to get back to the Academy before we somehow get caught up in another disaster.\"","Damien laughed.","A genuine laugh this time.","\"Yeah.\"","He nodded.","\"Me too.\"","The two young men sat quietly beside the window afterward.","Neither spoke for several minutes.","The morning sun continued rising higher into the sky.","Below them, the city carried on with its normal life.","For the first time since entering the dungeon, neither Noah nor Damien had to think about fighting.","Then Noah said with dejected voice. \"Damn! I had been more happy if I bad such talk with some beautiful girl like Lyria or Arisha.\"","Damien immediately replied with a laugh. \"Hahaha! Well I guess that’s expected from you...but you know what? You are one hell of a bastard!\""]},{"number":162,"title":"Chapter 162: Changes After Getting Bloodline","paragraphs":["Noah sat alone on a wooden bench inside the training hall.","The hall was relatively quiet at this hour. A few students could be seen training in the distance, while others chatted among themselves. Sunlight streamed through the tall windows, illuminating the polished floor.","Yet Noah paid attention to none of it.","His arms were folded across his chest, and his eyes remained glued to the translucent blue screen floating before him.","A wide grin slowly spread across his face.","The screen displayed something that made him happier than almost anything else.","Just two days ago, he had been fighting for his life.","At that time, he had only been at the Low Stage of the Awakened Core Rank.","He still remembered the terror of facing Marbas, the desperate battle, and the feeling of standing at death’s door.","But now things were completely different.","Somehow, after everything that had happened, he had broken through two stages in one go.","His Core Rank had reached the High Stage of Awakened.","That alone would have made most students celebrate for weeks.","However, that wasn’t what excited Noah the most.","There was something even more unbelievable.","Something that still made his blood boil with excitement whenever he thought about it.","The bloodline was Monarch of The Frost.","At first, Noah hadn’t paid much attention to it. There had simply been too many things happening.","The injuries, the mysterious system messages. The strange voice that had appeared.","The deaths of the students. The endless questioning from the academy instructors after they recovered.","All of it had left him mentally exhausted. Only after finally having some free time did he sit down and carefully examine his status.","And the results had nearly made him jump from the bench.","=== STATUS ===","Name: Noah Eldritch","Race: Human","Age: 19 Years","Strength: 260 [+158]","Speed: 247 [+142]","Stamina: 258 [+153]","Endurance: 235 [+145]","Charm: 612","Mana: 2553 [+1505]","Core Rank: Awakened (High)","Potential: Mythical Core / Origin Core (???)","Profession: [Combatant Lv.2]","Technique: [Frozen Lotus Blade Art], [Flowing String Archery]","Affinity: Ice","Spells: [Ice Shard], [Frost Bind], [Snow Mist]","Innate Ability: [Ice Creation]","Passive Ability: [Adaptive Learning]","Bloodline: [Monarch of The Frost]","=================","\"I can’t believe it...\" Noah muttered under his breath before shaking his head.","Then he laughed. \"I hit the jackpot!\"","And honestly, he wasn’t exaggerating. The increase in his stats alone was absurd. His mana had increased by an unbelievable amount.","His bloodline had awakened. And perhaps most importantly... His potential had changed.","It was now at Mythical Core. Also known as Origin Core.","Even though the system still displayed question marks, Noah understood one thing.","His future potential had reached an absurd level.","Only Damien had possessed potential on that level before.","The protagonist. The chosen hero. And now Noah’s name stood beside it. How could he not be happy?","His gaze briefly moved toward his Charm stat. The number was honestly ridiculous.","Noah snorted. \"Still useless.\"","Being handsome wouldn’t help him defeat demons.","Nor did he have any plans to become some womanizer.","Though... He couldn’t deny that teasing girls was surprisingly entertaining.","Especially when they reacted so easily.","\"Noah!\"","A familiar voice suddenly called out. The status window disappeared instantly. Noah turned his head.","A smile appeared on his face.","\"Mary.\"","She stood several meters away, looking much healthier than she had after escaping that nightmare.","Yesterday had been chaotic.","Every surviving student had been questioned by academy instructors regarding what happened inside the mysterious dungeon.","Because of that, Noah barely had a chance to talk with her.","\"Hello, Mary!\" Noah greeted cheerfully. \"What’s up? You okay?\"","Mary walked toward him before stopping nearby.","\"I’m okay,\" she replied softly.","Then her eyes narrowed slightly.","A faint smile appeared on her lips.","\"Seeing that huge smile on your face...\" she said while adjusting her glasses, \"...it seems something really good happened to you.\"","She tilted her head slightly.","\"You look happier than anyone else right now.\"","Noah chuckled.","\"Of course I’m happy.\"","He leaned back against the bench.","\"Everyone I care about survived.\"","His voice became quieter.","\"And more importantly...\"","A grin appeared again.","\"I survived.\"","Mary couldn’t help but laugh softly. \"That’s true.\"","However, her smile soon faded. Her gaze lowered toward the ground. For a few moments she remained silent.","Noah didn’t interrupt. He simply waited. Eventually Mary let out a small sigh. A faint blush appeared on her cheeks.","\"T-That day...\"","She nervously played with a strand of her hair.","\"While we were running...\"","Her voice became even quieter.","\"You held me in your arms and protected me from whatever was coming behind us.\"","The blush deepened.","\"I never got the chance to thank you properly.\"","She looked away.","\"So... thank you.\"","Noah blinked. He still remembered that moment. At the time, he hadn’t even thought about it.","His body had simply moved on instinct. Even now, he was slightly surprised by his own actions.","Still... Mary was his friend.","And after hearing those students dying behind him, he couldn’t bring himself to let the same thing happen to her.","A gentle smile appeared on Noah’s face.","\"You don’t need to thank me.\"","Mary slowly turned toward him. Their eyes met. Her black eyes behind the round glasses.","His blue eyes reflecting the afternoon sunlight that came from huge windows.","Noah’s expression softened.","\"You are my friend, Mary.\"","His voice was sincere.","\"A good friend.\"","He shrugged lightly.","\"How could I just stand there and watch something happen to you?\"","The smile on his face widened slightly.","\"My body moved before I could even think.\"","Mary’s cheeks turned even redder.","\"And honestly...\"","Noah scratched the back of his head.","\"I’m just happy you made it out safely.\"","Mary immediately looked away. Her heart skipped a beat.","For some reason Noah looked different lately. Maybe it was because he had grown stronger.","Maybe it was because of his recent experiences. Or maybe it was simply the confidence he carried now.","Whatever the reason, his smile felt strangely dangerous.","\"N-Noah!\"","She quickly pushed her glasses upward.","\"Don’t say things like that so casually!\"","Noah tilted his head. \"Hm?\"","Mary’s face grew even redder. \"T-They sound...\"","She struggled to finish her sentence. \"They sound...\"","Noah grinned.","\"How do they sound?\"","Mary immediately pointed a finger at him.","\"Argh! It’s weird!\"","She puffed her cheeks. \"You shouldn’t say things like that to girls so casually!\"","Noah burst into laughter. \"Hahaha!\"","Mary glared at him.","\"Stop laughing!\"","\"Okay, okay,\" Noah said while raising both hands in surrender. \"I won’t.\"","Mary narrowed her eyes suspiciously. She clearly didn’t believe him. A few moments later, Noah suddenly stood up.","\"Want to go for a walk?\"","Mary blinked for few seconds before nodding.","\"Hmm. Okay.\"","Together, they left the training hall.","The academy grounds were peaceful as evening slowly approached.","Students walked between buildings. Some trained on the open fields.","Others sat beneath trees enjoying the cool weather.","Noah and Mary simply walked side by side.","Then Noah suddenly spoke. \"You know, Mary...\"","\"Hm?\"","\"You look adorable when you’re embarrassed.\"","Mary nearly stumbled. Her entire body froze.Then she slowly turned toward him.","Her eyes narrowed behind her glasses. \"Noah.\"","\"Yes?\"","\"You’re doing it again.\"","Noah immediately started laughing.","\"Hehe~\"","\"What can I do?\" he asked innocently.","\"Your reactions are just too good.\"","\"Hmph!\"","Mary turned her head away. Her arms folded across her chest. A cute pout formed on her lips.","Noah couldn’t stop himself from smiling.","\"Hey.\"","No response.","\"I’m sorry.\"","There was only silence.","\"Mary?\"","She said nothing.","Noah rubbed his chin dramatically.","\"Hmm...If you don’t forgive me...\"","Mary glanced sideways.","\"...I’ll start talking like that again.\" Her eyes widened slightly.","Noah leaned closer.","\"Dear Mary~\"","\"Dammit, Noah!\"","Mary immediately snapped her head toward him.","\"Don’t do that!\"","Noah pointed at her triumphantly.","\"Look.\"","\"What?\"","\"You’re talking again.\"","Mary stared at him. Then groaned. \"You’re impossible.\"","The two continued walking through the academy campus while Noah quietly celebrated another successful victory.","After a while, Noah’s expression became thoughtful.","\"By the way...\"","Mary looked at him.","\"Hm?\"","\"How did you find that door?\"","He genuinely wanted to know. If not for Mary, they would all be dead.","Mary blinked.","\"Oh...\"","She looked slightly embarrassed.","\"That was because of my innate ability.\"","Noah listened carefully.","\"My ability allows me to observe things very closely.\"","She adjusted her glasses.","\"It’s nothing special.\"","Noah immediately disagreed.","\"It sounds special.\"","Mary smiled weakly.","\"My eyes are simply sharper than most people’s.\"","She looked forward while remembering that moment.","\"The wall looked normal to everyone else. But I noticed something different.\"","Her voice grew more confident.","\"A tiny difference in texture.It was almost impossible to see. But I could.\"","Noah whistled.","\"That’s actually amazing.\"","Mary smiled slightly.","\"Maybe...or not maybe.\"","Noah nodded firmly. \"It saved all of us.\"","A brief silence followed. Then Noah asked, \"So the door opened easily?\"","Mary thought for a moment before nodding. \"Yes. I used the last bit of strength I had.\"","Her expression became distant. \"And pushed. It opened immediately.\"","Noah laughed. \"Damn. We were lucky to have you.\"","Mary looked surprised.","Noah smiled. \"The real hero there was you. Everyone survived because you found that door.\"","Mary immediately shook her head.","\"No. That’s not true.\"","She looked at him seriously. \"If you all hadn’t fought the demon...If you hadn’t stalled him...I never would’ve had time to search.\"","She smiled softly. \"We survived because everyone worked together.\"","Noah nodded. \"True.\"","For a few moments, both of them simply walked in silence.","Then Mary suddenly spoke.","\"Hey, Noah?\"","\"Hm?\"","\"Can I ask you something?\"","Noah put his hands inside his pockets.","\"Sure.\"","Mary hesitated briefly.","Then she looked at him. \"Do you know why Ophelia seems to hate demons so much?\"","Noah blinked in surprise.","Mary adjusted her glasses.","\"Most people probably didn’t notice...But I did.\"","Her expression became thoughtful. \"She tried to hide it. But every time she looked at Marbas...\"","Mary’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"There was so much anger.\"","\"So much hatred.\"","She looked toward Noah. \"It felt personal.\"","A light breeze passed through the academy grounds. Noah’s expression slowly became serious.","Because unlike Mary... He actually had a pretty good idea why."]},{"number":163,"title":"Chapter 163: I’m here for you!","paragraphs":["Noah remained silent.","Not because he didn’t want to tell her. Rather, he was trying to remember what he knew about Ophelia’s past.","He let out a small sigh.","\"Hah... honestly, I don’t know the details. I mean, I don’t know exactly what happened. But I do know the overall story.\"","Myra looked at him curiously.","\"What is it?\" she asked.","Noah’s expression turned thoughtful.","\"Well... her mother was killed by demons when Ophelia was a child. Right in front of her own eyes. At least, that’s what I’ve heard. There was a demon invasion at her house... I don’t know why they did it.\"","He paused briefly before continuing.","\"Her mother was also someone strong and an exceptional sword user. But those demons were powerful. She lost her life while protecting Ophelia.\"","Mary covered her mouth in shock.","Her eyes behind her glasses trembled slightly.","\"I-I had no idea something like that happened to her.\"","Noah nodded.","\"Yes... neither did I. After that incident, she must have decided to take revenge on those demons... or demon. I don’t know the exact details, whether it was a single individual who killed her mother or multiple demons. Though Ophelia seems to know and wants to kill him... or them.\"","Mary’s expression slowly turned understanding.","\"Oh... no wonder she trains so hard.\"","\"Yes.\"","A trace of sadness appeared on Noah’s face.","\"Sadly, her little half-brother has better talent and potential. Because of that, it was clearly decided that he would become the future heir of the Thornveil House.\"","Then his expression became serious.","\"While Ophelia’s marriage was decided with me... the second son of the Eldritch Family.\"","Mary nodded slowly.","\"Yes... you two were engaged.\"","\"Damn, don’t use that word.\"","Noah frowned immediately.","\"We didn’t have any engagement ceremony. But well, it’s true that she was my fiancée. If a lady of a noble house doesn’t have the potential to become the heir, then her duty is to marry into a good family and strengthen connections.\"","Mary’s brows furrowed.","\"That’s really bad... a girl should have the choice of who she wants to be with. Though I understand how nobles think.\"","Noah let out a helpless chuckle.","\"Hah... she simply didn’t want to get married. And that’s why she always hated me. Not to mention how much of a waste of a man I was back then.\"","Myra glanced at him and shook her head slightly.","\"Hm... but you don’t look like that anymore.\"","A faint pink color appeared on her cheeks.","She quietly moved a few strands of hair behind her ear.","Noah chuckled while looking ahead.","His footsteps matched hers as they continued walking.","\"I am really happy to hear that from you.\"","A genuine smile appeared on his face.","\"Thank you.\"","Myra smiled softly.","\"You don’t need to thank me.\"","She hesitated briefly before speaking again.","\"So... did you really do that?\"","Noah blinked.","\"What?\"","She looked slightly uncomfortable.","\"I mean... the reason your engagement was broken.\"","\"Oh, that.\"","Noah’s smile faded a little.","\"Well, I won’t say it was false. It was true that I tried to force myself on her. But, you know... I liked her a lot back then.\"","He rubbed the back of his neck.","\"And at that time, I was really drunk. I pushed her onto a bed while saying things like ’I love you so much’ and other nonsense.\"","He shrugged.","\"But it was far from an assault.\"","\"Because...\"","Noah paused.","Myra looked at him attentively.","\"Because?\"","\"She was stronger than me back then.\"","A bitter smile appeared on his face.","\"Much stronger.\"","He continued calmly.","\"And I was so drunk that I barely knew what I was doing. At that time, she could have avoided me easily, pushed me aside, or even beaten me up.\"","Mary listened carefully.","Then suddenly her eyes widened as realization struck her.","\"So...\"","She hesitated.","\"Did she act like she was being assaulted? Like... some helpless girl?\"","A grin appeared on Noah’s face.","\"Ding dong! You got that right!\"","He pointed at her.","\"She did exactly that so she could break off the engagement. Then she could try again to become the heir and grow stronger to achieve her goal.\"","Mary’s expression became conflicted.","\"That’s... bad.\"","She lowered her gaze slightly.","\"I mean, what you did was wrong. But if she acted like that... then she was also wrong, since you suffered a lot because of her.\"","Noah immediately shook his head.","\"Don’t say that.\"","His voice became calm.","\"Whatever happened, I was wrong. I shouldn’t have done that, even if I was drunk.\"","He smiled faintly.","\"So let’s just say I received my punishment, and it’s all good now.\"","Noah looked noticeably more relaxed than before.","A small breath escaped him.","\"And I’m happy to share this with someone who actually cares about me.\"","He looked at Mary for a moment.","\"I wanted to tell this to someone... and now I feel much more relaxed.\"","Mary’s eyes softened.","A look of concern and closeness appeared on her face.","\"You...\"","She held his gaze.","\"You can always count on me. If there’s ever something you want to share, or a burden weighing on your heart, I’m here for you!\"","A gentle smile appeared on her lips.","\"I’ll always be willing to listen.\"","Noah was surprised to hear those words from her.","To be honest, it wasn’t really weighing on him.","That Noah was someone else.","The current Noah was a different person living inside Noah’s body.","He did feel some guilt.","But not that much.","More than guilt, he had simply felt annoyed and irritated.","He had wanted to tell someone.","That was all.","So he was genuinely shocked by how kind Mary was being.","She was willing to listen to his worries and sadness.","Even any that might come in the future.","Without realizing it, a genuine smile formed on his lips.","\"I’ll take you up on that offer then.\"","His smile widened slightly.","\"I hope you’ll listen to me in the future too.\"","Mary let out a cheerful laugh.","\"Hehe, of course I will.\"","The two of them continued talking as they walked through the academy streets together."]},{"number":164,"title":"Chapter 164: Possibilities","paragraphs":["Noah entered his dormitory room.","He was feeling slightly happy. After all, his conversation with Mary had left him in a better mood.","He headed straight to the bathroom to take a warm bath. He had been training earlier, and his body needed the rest.","A while later, he came out of the bathroom while drying his body with a towel.","He then jumped onto his bed and lay on his back.","His eyes stared at the ceiling.","A thoughtful expression appeared on his face.","’Hm... that thing was related to the Eternal Monarch... a Monarch to whom that demon was going to sacrifice students.’","He frowned slightly.","’Was that Monarch related to sacrifice, blood, or flesh...?’","Noah couldn’t tell exactly.","What he needed to do now was search for any information related to Monarchs.","If there was any. The second thing he needed to do was learn about secret organizations.","A thoughtful look settled on his face.","’A world like this must have some secret organizations...’","His eyes narrowed slightly.","’Some that are evil or act like cults... and others that work to protect the world, even if it means using evil methods.’","Noah sat up and walked over to his desk.","He pulled out the chair and sat down.","Then he took out the notebook where he had written information about the first two Acts of the game.","Now it was time for the Third Act.","He opened the notebook and started writing everything down in detail.","After finishing, his thoughts drifted toward Ophelia and the story of her mother.","A thoughtful expression crossed his face.","’She was supposed to be a hidden heroine...’","He tapped the notebook lightly with his finger. ’The protagonist could probably have her as a lover. At least, I think so.’","Noah then started thinking about how these kinds of stories usually unfolded.","A young woman seeking revenge against the demon who had killed her mother.","The first possibility that came to mind was the most common one.","He rested his chin on his hand while thinking. She would try to kill the demon herself.","Then, when she was on the verge of death, the protagonist would appear and save her.","Together they would fight the demon and kill him.","That was a very normal story route. Another possibility was a romance route. The protagonist could help her become stronger.","Or motivate her to keep moving forward.","Maybe he would even help her get rid of Noah, who was supposed to force himself on her after their engagement was broken.","Noah continued thinking.","Perhaps Noah would become obsessed with her, while Damien helped protect her.","But then he frowned.","’The real Noah died before the academy even started.’","He leaned back slightly in his chair.","’So that possibility shouldn’t count.’","A puzzled expression appeared on his face.","’But then again... it’s weird.’","His brows furrowed.","’A character like Noah should have stayed alive in the story for a while.’","The more he thought about it, the stranger it seemed.","’Someone obsessed with Ophelia...’","He narrowed his eyes.","’Someone who would eventually join the villains and become a minor antagonist.’","Noah tapped the desk thoughtfully.","’Then the protagonist would save Ophelia from him.’","Noah continued considering different possibilities for some time.","Unfortunately, he didn’t have enough information.","This was the best he could do for now.","Then a sudden realization crossed his mind.","\"Now that I think about it...\"","He muttered quietly to himself.","\"The next Act should be the first-semester exam...\"","That was usually how the story progressed after all.","A thoughtful expression appeared on his face again.","’Hmm...’","Then another thought suddenly entered his mind.","A slightly confused look appeared on his face.","’I have been doing so well...’","He paused.","’So why haven’t I received a call from my family?’","---","The atmosphere inside the principal’s office was unusually heavy.","Behind a large wooden desk sat Adrian, the principal of Novaris Academy.","His white old hair was neatly combed back, and his aged face carried a calm but serious expression.","The room was silent except for the ticking of a clock hanging on the wall.","Standing in front of him was Morgana Celestine.","She had just finished explaining everything that had happened during the field trip.","From the appearance of the suspicious demon to the ritual site hidden within the forest and the attempted sacrifice of students.","As she spoke, Adrian listened without interrupting a single time.","His fingers remained folded together on top of the desk while his sharp eyes stayed fixed on Morgana.","When she finally finished, silence filled the room.","A few moments passed before Adrian slowly leaned back in his chair.","His expression darkened.","\"This is bad...\" he said quietly.","Morgana’s brows furrowed.","Adrian’s eyes narrowed as he stared toward the window behind her.","\"It clearly indicates one thing.\"","A brief pause followed.","\"They are awakening slowly.\"","Morgana frowned.","For a second she didn’t understand who he was referring to.","Then realization struck her.","Her eyes immediately turned serious.","\"You mean...\" she said slowly. \"The Monarchs?\"","Adrian gave a grim nod.","\"Yes.\"","The single word carried an unsettling weight.","The room seemed to grow colder.","Morgana crossed her arms, her expression becoming increasingly troubled.","\"But there should be more time for it to happen...Isn’t this too earlier than expected?\"","\"Yes...it is,\" Adrian replied. \"At least for now. However, if demons are already conducting sacrifices in it’s names, then it means their influence is beginning to leak into the world again. Not all monarch need sacrifice..only few...or maybe one...only they need it.\"","Finally, Adrian stood from his chair. His expression was firm.","\"We don’t have the luxury of waiting.\"","He looked directly at Morgana.","\"Contact the Hero Association Council immediately.\"","His voice became stern.","\"We need an emergency meeting regarding this incident as soon as possible.\"","Morgana nodded.","\"I’ll do it right away.\"","The old principal turned toward the window once more.","His gaze drifted toward the distant horizon.","And for the first time in many years, genuine concern appeared in his eyes."]},{"number":165,"title":"Chapter 165: Meeting Between High Ranking Individuals (1)","paragraphs":["A city far away from Novaris City, where the academy was located.","This city was much larger in comparison.","Massive skyscrapers of steel and glass stretched high into the sky, their reflective surfaces shining beneath the afternoon sun. Wide roads crossed through the city like rivers of concrete, filled with countless vehicles moving in an organized flow.","People hurried along sidewalks, carrying briefcases, talking on phones, and moving toward their workplaces. The city never seemed to stop moving. It was a place where power, wealth, and influence gathered together.","This was Aurex Prime.","The capital city of the Aurelian Empire.","Overlooking the city from a distant hill stood a grand palace.","Its architecture was completely different from the modern skyline surrounding it. Ancient white stone walls, towering spires, and golden banners gave it an aura of timeless authority.","The Imperial Palace.","The residence of the Imperial Family. However, that place was not important today. Far from the palace, near the center of the city, stood another famous landmark.","A massive skyscraper rose above the surrounding buildings.","At its highest point, large silver letters were engraved across the structure.","[ HERO ASSOCIATION ]","The building was recognized throughout the empire. It was the headquarters of the organization responsible for protecting humanity from monsters, dungeons, and demonic threats.","At the very top floor of the skyscraper was a meeting hall. The room itself was enormous. A long rectangular table occupied the center.","Expensive wooden walls, crystal lights, and floor-to-ceiling windows gave the chamber an atmosphere of authority and prestige.","Several important individuals sat around the table.","People whose decisions could affect entire regions of the empire. At the head of the table sat an old man. His gray hair had begun turning white with age, yet his presence remained powerful.","Even while sitting, he carried an invisible pressure that filled the room. His eyes were sharp. His posture straight. His authority unquestionable.","He was Chester Grimspire. President of the Hero Association. One of the most influential figures in the entire empire.","The room remained silent as Chester’s gaze swept across everyone present.","\"You all may be wondering why you were called here so suddenly.\"","His deep voice echoed through the hall.","\"There is an important matter we must discuss.\"","A cold voice responded from across the table.","\"What kind of matter requires summoning even those who are not members of the Hero Association?\"","The tone was calm. It was not disrespectful.","But simply direct.","Chester’s eyes moved toward the speaker. There sat a handsome man in his mid-thirties.","His silver-white hair was neatly combed back. Purple eyes reflected confidence and composure. Even seated, he possessed the natural bearing of a ruler.","He was Duke Julian Eldritch. One of the most powerful nobles in the empire. The ruler of the vast Eldritch Dukedom. A territory so large and influential that many considered it a nation within the empire itself.","The Empire posses vast dukedoms, that’s why it’s called empire rather than kingdom.","Chester nodded slightly.","\"Duke Eldritch, your question is understandable.\"","His gaze traveled around the room.","\"I invited several noble houses because this matter concerns more than just the Hero Association.\"","A brief pause followed. \"Not all the dukes were able to attend, but three of you are here. That is sufficient.\"","His eyes shifted toward the man sitting beside Julian.","The man appeared to be around the same age. Dark midnight-colored hair framed a handsome face. His emerald eyes remained calm and observant.","He was Duke Lionel Thornveil. Ruler of the Thornveil Dukedom.","Lionel folded his hands calmly on the table. \"It was only natural for us to come.\"","His voice carried respect.","\"When someone of your position requests a meeting, ignoring it would be foolish.\"","Before Chester could respond, another voice interrupted.","\"Just begin already.\"","The voice was deeper. It felt like it belong to an old man.","More imposing. \"There is no need for unnecessary greetings.\"","Everyone’s attention shifted toward the opposite side of the table. An older man sat there wearing a simple black kimono. Unlike the luxurious suits worn by others, his clothing was plain.","Yet no one present dared underestimate him. His black hair contained several white streaks. Dark blue eyes remained sharp despite his age. He appeared to be in his late fifties.He was Duke Reiji Narukami.","One of the strongest swordsmen in the empire. The ruler of another dukedom. Which have culture far different compare to other regions of empire. His region was similar to japan.","His gaze briefly shifted toward Lionel Thornveil. Something flashed within his eyes. Gone before anyone could notice. As if there was something that made Reiji displeased at Lionel’s sight.","Chester simply nodded.","\"Very well.\"","Before he could continue, another person spoke.","\"It was I who requested this meeting.\"","All eyes turned toward Chester’s right side.","There sat Adrian.","Principal of Novaris Academy.","One of the empire’s most respected man.","Chester folded his hands.","\"Hmm.\"","\"It was indeed Adrian who requested this emergency meeting.\"","His expression grew serious.","\"There is something happening.\"","He looked toward Adrian.","\"You may explain now. Everyone is present.\"","Adrian nodded.","The atmosphere immediately became heavier.","\"All of you should already know about the attack that occurred shortly after the academy year began.\"","Several people nodded.","Everyone present had access to classified information.","\"The culprit was identified as Malrick.\"","Adrian paused.","\"But that is not all.\"","His expression darkened.","\"A week ago, our students were attacked again.\"","The room became silent.","\"This time during a field trip near Oakhaven.\"","Duke Julian’s eyes narrowed slightly.","He had heard reports regarding the incident.","Most of the others had as well.","Adrian continued.","\"What was not revealed to the public is what our investigation discovered afterward.\"","The room seemed to grow colder.","The principal’s voice became quieter.","\"They were conducting a ritual.\"","No one interrupted.","\"A sacrifice.\"","Several expressions changed.","Then Adrian spoke the final words.","\"A sacrifice intended for a ... Monarch. At least that’s what i think so...\"","There was complete silence.","Even Duke Reiji’s expression hardened.","The word Monarch carried a terrifying meaning. Ancient beings that could rival gods in powers Existences whose names were associated with disasters, destruction, and extinction.","Lionel Thornveil frowned.","\"Are you certain?\"","\"No.\"","Adrian answered honestly.","\"But all evidence points toward that conclusion.\"","Chester slowly nodded.","\"Continue.\"","Adrian took a breath.","\"Not only that.\"","His eyes shifted toward Julian.","\"Duke Eldritch.\"","Julian met his gaze.","\"Your son, Noah Eldritch, along with several companions, explored a dungeon recently.\"","Julian’s expression remained calm.","Though inwardly he was surprised.","\"What about it?\"","\"They discovered a massive underground pit.\"","The room listened carefully. Adrian’s voice grew grave \"Inside were hundreds of creatures.. Only hero Association and academy knows about this.\"","Several brows furrowed.","\"Hundreds?\"","Lionel repeated.","Adrian nodded.","\"Hundreds.\"","His next words sent another chill through the room.","\"They were asleep.\"","The silence deepened.","\"Neither our records nor our databases contain information about those creatures.\"","Julian’s expression finally changed slightly.","\"Unknown monsters?\"","\"Possibly.\"","Adrian shook his head.","\"Or perhaps something else entirely.\"","Chester folded his hands beneath his chin.","The old man’s eyes had become incredibly serious.","\"An academy attack, a demonic sacrifice and unknown creatures.\"","He spoke each point separately.","Then slowly exhaled.","\"All within a few months.\"","Nobody disagreed.","Because when viewed together, the incidents formed a disturbing pattern.","Lionel’s expression darkened.","\"You believe these events are connected.\"","\"I do.\"","Adrian answered immediately.","\"If these incidents were isolated, I would not have requested this meeting.\"","His gaze swept across the room.","\"But they are occurring too frequently.\"","\"Something is changing.\"","Duke Reiji remained silent for several moments.","Then he finally spoke.","\"If related to Monarchs are truly involved...\"","His deep voice echoed through the chamber.","\"Then we may already be too late.\"","Those words made the room even heavier.","Chester narrowed his eyes.","\"No.\"","His voice was firm.","\"We are not at that stage yet.\"","He rose from his seat.","Immediately, everyone’s attention focused on him.","The President of the Hero Association looked around the room.","\"We will begin a full investigation.\"","His voice carried authority.","\"Every suspicious organization. Every cult. Every unusual dungeon activity. Every demon movement.\"","His eyes sharpened. \"I want reports on everything.\"","No one objected. Because everyone understood the stakes. If Monarchs were truly beginning to awaken...","Then the peace humanity had enjoyed for decades might soon come to an end.","And for the first time during the meeting.","Every person present felt the same unsettling thought. A storm was coming."]},{"number":166,"title":"Chapter 166: Meeting Between High Ranking Individuals (2)","paragraphs":["\"The reason I wanted you nobles to come here today is exactly because of this.\"","Chester’s deep voice echoed throughout the meeting hall.","His sharp gaze swept across every person seated around the table.","\"I want all of you to focus on your respective regions. Increase surveillance and investigations. Look into any newly formed organizations, any suspicious groups, any unusual activities in the underworld, and any hidden powers that may be growing in the shadows.\"","His expression grew stern.","\"Anything suspicious. No matter how insignificant it may seem. I want reports on it.\"","The room remained silent as everyone listened carefully.","\"Also...\"","Chester folded his hands on the table.","\"From this moment onward, remain cautious.\"","Every noble and high-ranking hero present understood the seriousness behind those words.","One by one, they nodded.","Even the usually relaxed heroes had become noticeably serious.","Near the corner of the table sat Morgana Celestine.","She had remained silent throughout most of the meeting, simply listening to the discussion unfold.","Chester leaned back slightly in his chair.","\"Honestly, the Pope would know more about matters related to Monarchs than any of us.\"","A few people nodded in agreement.","\"Unfortunately, he is currently occupied with another matter and was unable to attend today’s meeting.\"","His eyes narrowed slightly.","\"But we will speak with him later.\"","One of the S-Rank Heroes sitting near the center of the table raised a question.","\"Do we know where Malrick is currently?\"","The man’s expression was serious.","\"And if I remember correctly, Cedric was involved with him as well.\"","Several eyes turned toward Chester.","The old man nodded.","\"Duke Nightfall is currently handling that matter.\"","His voice remained calm.","\"He is personally searching for any traces of Cedric Nightfall.\"","A brief pause followed.","\"After all... Cedric is his younger brother.\"","A faint snort came from one side of the table.","\"Good.\"","The speaker was Marquis Stormbane.","A rugged middle-aged man with a scar running across his jaw.","\"Knowing the relationship between those two, Duke Nightfall is probably furious.\"","A few people silently agreed.","\"If anyone wants Cedric dead the most, it would be his own brother.\"","Duke Lionel Thornveil spoke calmly from his seat.","His emerald eyes remained composed.","\"Cedric has spent years tarnishing the Nightfall Family’s reputation.\"","\"Indeed.\"","Chester nodded once.","Then his expression changed.","Something darker entered his gaze.","\"There is another matter.\"","Immediately, everyone’s attention focused on him. The old man slowly folded his hands together.","\"Recently, we discovered information regarding a certain organization.\"","The room grew quieter.","\"What kind of organization?\" someone asked.","Chester’s eyes became serious. \"What we know is limited.\"","A brief pause. \"But one fact has already been confirmed.\"","His next words caused the atmosphere to freeze. \"The organization contains vampires.\"","There was complete silence. Several people stiffened. Even Adrian’s eyes widened slightly.","This was the first time he had heard this information.","Chester continued. \"Whether it is merely a group containing vampires...\"","His gaze swept across the room.","\"Or an entire organization made up exclusively of vampires...\"","The old man slowly shook his head. \"We don’t know.\"","No one spoke for several moments.","The revelation had been unexpected.","Monarchs. Demon doing sacrifices, uknown creatures. And now vampires.","The list of problems continued growing.","Finally, Chester exhaled.","\"It seems today’s meeting will be longer than any of us expected.\"","No one disagreed.","---","While Important meeting was going on in other city.","Back to the academy.","It’s been a week since the events of the Oakhaven incident had already passed. Life at Novaris Academy had slowly returned to normal. At least on the surface.","Noah stepped out of his dormitory room. His hands rested casually inside his pockets as he walked through the hallway. Earlier that morning, he had received a message from the administrative office.","Someone had come to meet him. Naturally, Noah had been confused. Who would come all the way to Novaris Academy to meet him?","At first, he considered the possibility that it might be someone from his family. But he quickly dismissed the idea.","If a family member were planning to visit, they would have informed him beforehand through a call or message. At least that was what he thought.","A few minutes later, Noah arrived at the designated meeting area. The moment he saw the visitor, his steps paused.","His eyes widened slightly. ’So it really is someone from my family.’","Standing a short distance away was a handsome young man who looked to be around twenty-six years old.","His wheat-blond hair was neatly styled.","Sharp purple eyes carried a familiar confidence.","The resemblance was obvious. They shared the same eyes. The same facial structure.","The same noble appearance. The man smiled the moment he noticed Noah.","\"There you are.\" His voice carried a warm familiarity.","\"Long time no see, Noah.\" The smile widened.","\"How have you been?\"","Noah stared at him for a moment. Then recognition fully settled in.","’My older brother... Nathan Eldritch.’ Just a week ago, Noah had been wondering why nobody from the Eldritch Family had contacted him.","And now his older brother was standing right in front of him. Life really had a strange sense of timing.","Fragments of memory surfaced in his mind.","Unlike many noble families, the relationship between Noah and Nathan had always been surprisingly normal.","There was no rivalry. No hidden hostility. Nor there was any struggle for inheritance. Nathan had simply acted like an older brother.","And Noah had acted like a younger one. But spoiled one. Noah ran a hand through his hair before shaking his head with a small laugh.","\"I’m doing well, brother.\"","A curious look appeared on his face. \"What about you?\"","He narrowed his eyes slightly. \"And more importantly...\"","A grin appeared. \"You came all the way here without informing me first.\"","Nathan immediately laughed. \"Haha.\"","He spread his hands. \"I wanted to surprise you.\"","Then he walked forward and lightly patted Noah’s shoulder. \"Looks like it worked.\"","Noah rolled his eyes. \"Unfortunately.\"","\"Hah!\"","Nathan laughed again. Then he glanced toward the academy grounds.","\"So.\"","He clasped his hands behind his back. \"How about we go somewhere more comfortable and talk?\"","His gaze drifted toward the distant café building. \"Let’s grab some coffee.\"","A nostalgic smile appeared on his face.","\"It’s been years since I graduated from this academy.\" His eyes softened slightly.","\"I suddenly feel like drinking coffee there again.\"","Noah looked in the same direction. Then a smirk slowly appeared on his lips.","\"Normally...I only accept coffee invitations from girls.\"","Nathan blinked.","\"But...\"Noah sighed heavily. \"Since you’re my brother, I’ll make an exception.\"","For a second there was silence. Then, \"Hahahaha!!\" Nathan burst into loud laughter.","Several nearby students turned to look. \"My brother really is generous.\" He wiped the corner of his eye.","\"What a great honor.\" Noah grinned.","\"You’re welcome.\"","The two brothers looked at each other. Then, side by side, they began walking toward the academy café.","For the first time in a long while, Noah found himself genuinely curious about what his family had to say."]},{"number":167,"title":"Chapter 167: Talk with Brother and Progress","paragraphs":["\"So, how’s your academy life, Noah?\"","Nathan asked with a relaxed smile while taking a sip of his coffee.","Noah leaned back slightly in his chair.","\"Hmm. Everything is good.\"","Nathan nodded with understanding expression.","\"I heard about and saw your records. You are doing really amazing. Your performance is far better than Father and I ever expected. Not only that, you even contributed during the attack that occurred at the academy. That’s really great.\"","Noah chuckled lightly.","\"Haha, thank you for the compliments. And I am really working hard.\"","Nathan looked at him carefully before nodding again.","\"Hmm, I know that. I can see it.\"","A thoughtful expression appeared on his face.","\"And even your personality has changed a lot. If it were the old you, you would have shown anger toward me rather than joking around.\"","Noah smiled faintly.","\"Change was needed. So I changed.\"","He shrugged.","\"And I feel much better now. I even made new friends.\"","A pleased smile appeared on Nathan’s face.","\"Good to hear that.\"","Noah hesitated briefly before asking.","\"So... how’s Mother? Is she... still angry?\"","Nathan immediately laughed.","\"Of course. She’s still angry.\"","He shook his head while chuckling.","\"Haha.\"","Then his expression softened.","\"But I think if you continue to be like this... her anger might calm down.\"","Noah nodded.","\"Okay... I will try my best.\"","Then he narrowed his eyes.","\"But why are you here? Don’t tell me you came just to talk and meet me after such a long time.\"","Nathan rubbed the back of his neck.","\"Hey, I really did want to meet you. That’s why I came.\"","Then his expression became slightly serious.","\"Also, there’s something else I wanted to tell you.\"","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\"What is it?\"","Nathan smiled.","\"After a lot of convincing, Mother allowed you to visit home.\"","He paused briefly.","\"So come home during the summer holidays after your first semester ends.\"","Noah was visibly surprised.","His eyes widened slightly.","Then he nodded.","\"Okay.\"","A small smile appeared on his face.","\"Okay. I’ll come.\"","There was no reason for Noah to refuse.","He didn’t hold any anger toward his family.","’I might be able to get some money from my family during that time.’","A thoughtful expression appeared on his face.","’And unlike the old Noah, I can finally learn properly from Father during the holidays.’","Noah nodded to himself before looking back at Nathan.","\"Is that all you wanted to say?\"","He tilted his head slightly.","\"Is that why you came to meet me?\"","Nathan went silent for a few moments.","Then he sighed.","\"Actually, there’s another reason.\"","He shook his head.","\"But you don’t need to worry about it.\"","A small smile appeared on his face.","\"I have something to do with the academy. That’s the primary reason I came.\"","Noah simply nodded.","\"Oh, okay.\"","He didn’t ask what that reason was.","Then a teasing smile appeared on his face.","\"So meeting me wasn’t your primary objective.\"","He pointed at Nathan dramatically.","\"I was just a side quest.\"","Nathan immediately rolled his eyes.","\"Hey, don’t say that.\"","Noah laughed.","The two brothers continued talking for a while.","Eventually, Noah stood up from his chair.","\"Since you have work to do, I’ll get going now.\"","He stretched his arms slightly.","\"I’m heading to training.\"","Then he looked at Nathan.","\"Also, when you’re done with whatever you came here for, call me. I’ll come meet you before you leave.\"","Nathan nodded.","\"Sure.\"","A proud smile appeared on his face.","\"You can go and work hard.\"","Noah waved casually before leaving the café.","Nathan remained seated for a while.","Leaning back in his chair, he quietly stared through the large glass wall.","His thoughts seemed distant.","Then a voice suddenly interrupted his silence.","\"So, how does he look now?\"","The voice was calm.","\"Your brother.\"","A figure approached the table.","Nathan looked up.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"He changed.\"","He shook his head in disbelief.","\"Changed a lot.\"","His gaze drifted toward the direction Noah had left.","\"I can’t believe he’s the same little brother I know.\"","The newcomer sat down in the seat Noah had occupied only a few minutes ago. A familiar academy uniform came into view.","It was Victor. The weapon arts instructor of Novaris Academy.","Victor folded his arms. \"I guess you’re happy seeing him in a better state.\"","Nathan nodded. \"What about you?\" He looked directly at Victor. \"You’re his weapon arts instructor.\"","Victor leaned back slightly.","\"I have to say...\"","A small smile appeared on his face.","\"Your brother has really changed.\"","His eyes narrowed thoughtfully.","\"And he’s getting stronger day by day.\"","Nathan chuckled.","\"I am happy to hear that.\"","Then his expression became serious.","\"So.\"","He lowered his voice.","\"What exactly is going on?\"","His eyes sharpened.","\"Did you find anything during the incident in the forests near Oakhaven City?\"","Victor immediately sighed.","Suddenly, an invisible dome-like barrier formed around their table. The surrounding sounds disappeared. The barrier ensured that nobody could hear their conversation.","Victor rubbed his forehead. \"We’re in a public place.\" His expression became annoyed. \"Don’t ask things like that out of nowhere.\"","Nathan coughed awkwardly. \"Oh, sorry.\" He smiled sheepishly. \"I really wanted to know about it.\"","Victor simply nodded. Then his expression became serious. \"Boss said it was a lesser form of an Eternal Monarch.\"","Nathan’s eyes widened.","\"What?\"","He leaned forward.","\"So... that thing was really a Monarch?\"","Victor nodded.","\"Yes.\"","His voice remained calm.","\"It only appeared for less than a minute.\"","A serious look crossed his face.","\"Most of its power had been used to open the portal... It’s amusing as it actually decided go show up on the calling of some normal demon. It means... it actually want to enter this world. But it’s still hard. It was lesser form not true. \"","He paused.","\"And if not for our boss being present there...\"","Victor’s expression darkened.","\"The situation could have become much worse.\"","Nathan clenched his teeth. \"And my brother survived something like that.\"","Victor nodded again.","\"Yes.\"","Then he stood up.","\"Let’s move.\"","His eyes shifted toward the exit.","\"Boss is waiting for you.\"","Nathan immediately stood. The invisible barrier dissolved. The sounds of the café returned. Without saying anything further, both men left the café.","And headed toward an unknown destination.","---","Noah, completely unaware of what Nathan and Victor had been discussing.","Or who exactly they were referring to as Boss.","He walked carefree toward the training grounds. Standing in the open field, he raised one hand.","A focused expression appeared on his face. Mana inside his core began moving rapidly throughout his body.","The air around him suddenly grew colder. Then weapons made entirely of ice started forming around him.","This time not six or not even ten. But nearly thirty weapons appeared within a few seconds.","They were words, spears and daggers and axes.","Floating silently in the air.Ready to launch at Noah’s command. A wide grin spread across his face.","\"Damn, this is amazing.\"He looked genuinely excited. \"It’s definitely the effect of my bloodline.\"","At first, Noah had wondered what exactly his bloodline did. Was its only effect breaking his potential limit?","Apparently not.His Innate Ability, Ice Creation. Had become far easier and more efficient to use.","Previously, he had needed to concentrate on every detail of whatever he wanted to create.","The shape, the structure and balance, everything, he needed to focus on it.","Now it was different.All he needed to do was think about it. Give a command. And the ice would automatically form whatever he desired.","It was perfect. As though the ice itself understood what he wanted.","Not only that. The amount of mana required had decreased significantly.","A huge advantage.Noah moved his hand.The weapons instantly shot through the air. Their movements were smooth and incredibly fast.","One by one, they flew around the training field like obedient soldiers.","Noah controlled each weapon individually. And the strain on his brain had also decreased greatly.","Which was another huge benefit.\"Haha!\"","His grin widened. \"This is going to be fun.\"","Several nearby students stopped their training.They looked upward in shock. Dozens of crystalline weapons danced through the sky.","Almost like a performance.Like some grand magical spectacle.","Then Noah snapped his fingers.","Crack.","All the weapons shattered instantly. Countless tiny particles of ice scattered through the air before disappearing.","Noah exhaled in satisfaction.\"My ability is getting better and better every day...\"","A confident smile appeared on his face. \"And Adaptive Learning helps with everything.\"","\"Status Window.\"","=== STATUS ===","Name: Noah Eldritch","Race: Human","Age: 19 Years","Strength: 262 [+2]","Speed: 241 [+1]","Stamina: 260 [+2]","Endurance: 236 [+1]","Charm: 612","Mana: 2573 [+20]","Core Rank: Awakened (High)","Potential: Mythical Core / Origin Core (???)","Profession: [Combatant Lv.2]","Technique: [Frozen Lotus Blade Art], [Flowing String Archery]","Affinity: Ice","Spells: [Ice Shard], [Frost Bind], [Snow Mist]","Innate Ability: [Ice Creation]","Passive Ability: [Adaptive Learning]","Bloodline: [Monarch of Frost]","=================","Noah clicked on the technique section.","Immediately, his progress appeared.","---","===","[Frozen Lotus Blade Art]","[First Petal: Dewdrop Stance] >>> (Proficiency: 97%)","[Flowing String Archery]","[First Form - Still Calm Strike] >>> (Proficiency: 99%)","===","A satisfied smile appeared on his face.","\"Good...\"","He nodded.","\"Now I need to start learning the other forms of the techniques.\"","Without wasting any time, Noah pulled his sword from his storage ring.","His eyes gleamed with excitement.","It was time to continue training the first form of his blade technique before moving on to the second.","And he was genuinely looking forward to it.","---","[A/N:Guys! If you haven’t read my first novel yet then go and read it. Well not forcing you guys, but it’s my first work. So would very happy if you guys tried reading it.]"]},{"number":168,"title":"Chapter 168: Group Study","paragraphs":["Three weeks later.","Noah was walking through one of the academy corridors with two young men.","One of them was a giant of a man, standing well over two hundred centimeters tall. He was none other than Draven.","Beside him walked a gray-haired beastman with black-striped cat ears on top of his head. Most people considered him a cat beastman.","However, he was actually a tiger beastman.","Though Noah always insisted that cats and tigers belonged to the same family anyway.","Draven suddenly let out a long sigh.","\"I cannot understand it... This is too much.\"","His heavy voice carried more frustration than usual.","Currently, even someone as carefree as Draven looked nervous and worried.","Ragnar immediately nodded in agreement.","\"I know, right?\"","He threw his hands into the air dramatically.","\"I still don’t understand why we need to study all this difficult stuff. Studying itself was already bad enough, but why are there written exams too?!\"","Noah placed a hand on Ragnar’s shoulder and spoke in the tone of a wise adult.","\"I can feel your pain, young man.\"","Ragnar looked at him blankly.","Noah nodded seriously.","\"But we have to do what we need to do.\"","Draven frowned.","\"Why?\"","He clenched his fist.","\"Can’t we just fight each other for marks? The winner gets the points.\"","Noah chuckled.","\"We’ll need to do something similar during the first-semester practical exam.\"","He shrugged.","\"I mean, there will be fighting involved.\"","Ragnar immediately moved closer. His expression became pleading. \"Hey, Noah. Help me study.\"","His voice was full of desperation.","\"I really need a tutor.\"","Draven’s eyes lit up.","\"Me too!\"","He pointed at Noah.","\"Teach me as well.\"","Noah looked at both of them with disbelief.","\"Hah...\"","He rubbed his forehead.","\"You guys really think I’m good at studying?\"","\"At least you’re better than us.\"","Ragnar replied instantly.","Noah paused.","Then nodded.","\"Well... I can’t deny that.\"","Currently, the three of them were heading toward the library. Normally, Noah spent most of his time alone.","He was completely dedicated to training. Every day he pushed himself until his body was exhausted.","Most of his training sessions were done alone, though occasionally he sparred with Damien. Usually, those matches were fought using only weapons, without spells or abilities.","Today, however, these two had suddenly dragged him away.","Because they were desperate. Although they belonged to different classes, Ragnar and Draven were still good friends of his.","\"Hey, you three idiots.\"","A familiar voice suddenly echoed through the corridor behind them. The trio immediately turned around.","Noah looked left and right.","\"Oh?\"","A teasing smile appeared on his face. \"Where are these three idiots?\"","Draven blinked. \"Who are these idiots?\"","He sounded genuinely curious.","Ragnar crossed his arms.","\"Well, there are many idiots in this academy.\"","He nodded thoughtfully.","\"We can’t really tell who she means.\"","While the three of them were busy discussing the identity of the mysterious idiots, the person behind them let out a long breath.","Arisha stood there with her arms folded beneath her chest. A look of pure disappointment appeared on her face.","\"Really?\"","Her eyebrow twitched.","\"There is only one group of three people standing in this corridor.\"","She stared directly at them.","\"So who exactly do you think I might be talking about?\"","Then her eyes landed on Noah.","\"And Noah.\"","Her voice became flatter.","\"You were the one who messaged me and said you needed help.\"","Ragnar looked shocked.","\"Did she just call me an idiot?\"","Draven looked equally offended.","\"She called me an idiot too?\"","Then Ragnar suddenly looked at Noah.","While Noah said, \"Wait.\" His eyes widened. \"How can you call your boyfriend an idiot?\"","\"The hell?!\"","Regnar nearly choked.","\"When did that happen?\"","Draven nodded seriously.","\"Hah.\"","His expression became one of admiration.","\"Noah is amazing.\"","He placed a hand over his chest.","\"He is a real man.\"","His respect for Noah increased dramatically.","Arisha rolled her eyes.","\"Whatever.\"","She looked at Noah. \"Why did you call me?\"","Noah coughed lightly. \"You know exams are near.\"","\"Yes.\"She nodded.\"And?\"","\"We three are having problems.\" Noah pointed at her.","\"You’re really smart when it comes to theory.\"","Then he smiled.","\"So I was hoping you’d help us.\"","Immediately, Ragnar and Draven turned toward Arisha. Both wore pleading expressions.","Arisha stared at them for several moments. Then she sighed.","\"And what exactly do I get in return for helping you three?\"","Without hesitation, Noah pointed at himself. \"A date with me.\"","He spoke as though he were offering a priceless treasure.","Arisha answered instantly. \"Don’t want it.\"","Her indifferent expression never changed.","\"Tch!\"","Ragnar immediately seized the opportunity. \"Noah, your girl doesn’t even want a date with you.\"","He shook his head dramatically.","\"Tsk. Tsk.\"","Draven nodded like a wise scholar. \"A man should never bargain with his woman by using date .\"","His expression was extremely serious.","\"You cannot trade a date with her.\"","He raised one finger.","\"It is her right to have a date with you whenever she wishes.\"","Noah stared at both of them with a deadpan expression. These two seriously believed Arisha was his girlfriend.","Couldn’t they understand it was just a joke?","What was even crazier was that Arisha wasn’t trying to correct them. She simply stood there with her arms folded and a calm expression.","Noah sighed and rubbed his face.","\"Just help us.\"","He looked genuinely defeated. \"We’ll do whatever you ask us to do.\"","Arisha nodded with satisfaction. \"Good boy.\"","Then she turned toward the library. \"Let’s go.\"","And so, the four of them headed toward the library.","---","\"Seriously?\"","Arisha pinched the bridge of her nose.","\"I am becoming dumber while teaching you two.\"","Currently, the four sat around a table in one corner of a private study room inside the library.","Noah had immediately taken the opportunity to sit beside her.","Meanwhile, Draven and Ragnar sat across from them.","\"It’s too hard!\" Ragnar grabbed his head with both hands.","He looked like a man suffering from a life-threatening illness.","\"Hmm.\"","Draven stared at the textbook in front of him.","\"It seems I will fail the written exam.\"","He nodded seriously. \"Well then.\" He closed the book. \"No need to study anymore.\"","The textbook looked like an enemy he could never defeat.","At least Noah was doing much better. He glanced at the duo and shook his head.","’Arisha’s teaching is actually really good.’","He looked at Ragnar.Then at Draven.","’The problem isn’t her. They simply aren’t at the level of average students when it comes to studying.’","Meanwhile, Arisha had not given up.","Not yet. She opened the mana theory textbook.","\"Listen carefully.\"","Her expression became serious.","\"I’ll explain it again.\"","Ragnar and Draven immediately straightened in their seats.","\"Mana exists naturally in the world.\"","She decided to teach them from basics that even kids have knowledge about.","Arisha pointed at a diagram inside the book.","\"The body absorbs mana through the mana core.\"","She looked directly at Ragnar.","\"What happens if a person tries to use more mana than their core can handle forcefully?\"","Ragnar thought for a few moments.","Then his eyes brightened.","\"They become stronger?\"","Arisha stared at him.","\"No.\"","\"Oh.\"","Ragnar lowered his head.","Draven raised his hand confidently. \"They explode?\"","Arisha closed her eyes. \"...Still no.\"","Noah quietly turned away to hide his laughter.","After a few seconds, Arisha continued. \"They suffer mana backlash.\"","She pointed at the diagram again. \"The mana channels become damaged.\"","This time both boys nodded. They seemed to understand. At least a little.","\"Good.\"","That’s how she started to teach them from basic to slowly led them toward the topic they need to learn."]},{"number":169,"title":"Chapter 169: Helping a Cat","paragraphs":["After a hour.","Arisha flipped to another Chapter. \"Now let’s talk about simple potion making.\"","Immediately, both boys looked terrified. \"No...\"","Ragnar whispered. \"Not potions...\"","Arisha ignored him. \"There are three basic steps.\"","She began writing on a sheet of paper.","\"Ingredient preparation.Mana infusion. Stabilization.\"","Noah listened quietly. Even he found the explanation useful.","Making mana potion was important. It comes under the basic survival in forest. It could be very useful. One could create healing potion with right ingredients.","Arisha continued patiently.","\"For example, a basic recovery potion requires Moonleaf, Blue Root, and purified mana water.\"","Draven blinked.","\"What happens if I accidentally add double the ingredients?\"","Arisha looked at him.","\"It explodes.\"","Draven immediately wrote that down. \"Very important information.\"","Ragnar nodded seriously. \"Agreed.\"","Arisha sighed again.","Then she continued teaching.","And despite all her complaints, she patiently explained mana theory and potion making again and again.","Until even Ragnar and Draven slowly began understanding.","At least enough to survive the upcoming written exams.","Which, for those two, was already a miracle.","---","After more than three hours of teaching, those two had finally managed to learn something.","Ragnar suddenly threw both of his arms into the air and laughed loudly.","\"Hahaha! This was easier than I had thought!\"","Beside him, Draven folded his arms confidently and nodded.","\"Hmm... I guess I can pass this exam with flying colors.\"","The two had completely changed their attitudes after finally understanding a few concepts.","Across from them, Arisha slumped back against her chair with a tired expression.","Her golden eyes stared at the duo as if they were the most ridiculous people she had ever met.","Noah simply watched them with a deadpan expression.","Then he let out a sigh.","\"Anyways.\"","He turned his head toward Arisha.","\"How did I do?\"","Arisha looked at him for a moment. Then a very small, soft smile appeared on her face.","\"You were my light today.\"","Her gaze briefly shifted toward Ragnar and Draven.","\"While I was surrounded by the darkness of these two.\"","Noah chuckled softly. ’It was really helpful having her teach us.’","His eyes drifted toward the books on the table.","’The lessons felt much easier. It would have taken me far longer to learn everything by myself.’","Just then, Arisha slowly extended her hand toward him.","Noah blinked.","A second later, her palm landed on top of his soft, silky silver-white hair.","Noah’s entire body visibly stiffened.","His eyes widened in shock.","Arisha leaned slightly closer, a gentle smile still resting on her face. Then she gently stroked his head.","\"You were a good boy today, Noah.\"","Her voice was calm and soft.","\"You did well. Good work.\"","\"H-Hey!!\"","Noah immediately raised his voice in surprise.","\"What are you doing?!\"","Caught completely off guard by her actions, he leaned backward in his chair, trying to create some distance between them.","Unfortunately, Arisha had no intention of letting him escape.","She leaned forward slightly and continued stroking his hair.","A visible blush quickly formed on Noah’s cheeks.","Meanwhile, Ragnar and Draven watched the entire scene with great amusement.","Their eyes widened.","\"Ohhhhh!!!\"","Draven exclaimed dramatically.","At the same time,","Whistle~","Ragnar let out a teasing whistle.","Draven pointed toward the pair with a knowing expression.","\"This is love.\"","\"Yes.\"","Ragnar nodded immediately.","\"This is definitely love.\"","Noah instantly turned toward them with a slightly red face.","\"This is not!\"","His protest only made them grin even more.","Meanwhile, Arisha completely ignored Ragnar and Draven’s comments.","Instead, she continued gently patting Noah’s head.","A faint smile lingered on her lips.","Clearly, she was enjoying Noah’s embarrassed reaction far more than she should have.","And judging from the growing blush on Noah’s face, that only made it worse.","\"Okay that’s enough.\" He said while shaking his head.","As much as he loves to get his head pat by her.","It was shameful to do it in public. Especially in front of his two friends.","Arisha was satisfied so she took her hand away from his head.","Finally he was free.","----","Evening had already arrived by the time Noah left the library.","The orange glow of the setting sun painted the academy grounds in warm colors. Long shadows stretched across the pathways while a cool breeze drifted through the trees.","Arisha had already gone toward the girls’ dormitory after their study session ended.","Meanwhile, Ragnar and Draven had remained behind in the study room, apparently determined to review everything they had learned before their newfound knowledge disappeared.","That left Noah walking alone.","His hands rested inside his pockets as he made his way toward the boys’ dormitory.","The academy grounds were relatively quiet at this hour. A few students passed by here and there, chatting with friends or heading back to their dorms after training.","Noah was enjoying the peaceful atmosphere.","Rustle.","A faint sound came from somewhere nearby.","Noah stopped.","His eyes shifted toward a cluster of bushes growing beside a grassy lawn near the path.","\"Hm?\"","Another rustle followed.","Curious, Noah stepped off the pathway and walked closer.","The leaves parted slightly.","And something small emerged from inside.","A black cat.","Noah blinked.","Immediately, he recognized her.","The sleek black fur. The vivid yellow eyes with narrow vertical pupils.","The same elegant little creature he and Arisha had encountered before.","\"The cat.\"","A small smile appeared on his face.","However, the smile quickly faded. Something was wrong. The cat was limping.","One of her front legs was injured.","Every step she took looked painful.","The usually graceful creature moved much slower than before.","Noah’s expression softened.","\"Hey...\"","He slowly crouched down.For a moment, the cat stared at him. Her yellow eyes narrowed slightly.","Noah carefully extended his hand.","Surprisingly she didn’t hiss this time.","She didn’t run away either. Perhaps she was too tired and was in pain.","Or perhaps the injury had made her lower her guard.","Whatever the reason, she simply watched him.","Noah carefully slid one hand beneath her body.","Then gently lifted her. The cat gave a small sound of protest.","\"Meow.\"","But she didn’t struggle.","Noah glanced down at the injured leg. His brows furrowed.","\"Looks like you got yourself into trouble.\"","The cat merely stared at him.","Noah shook his head. Then a small smile appeared on his face.","\"Don’t worry, cat.\"","His voice was calm and reassuring.","\"I’ll help you.\"","The cat blinked once. That was her only response.","Noah adjusted his grip carefully so he wouldn’t hurt her injured leg.","Then he stood up.","The black cat rested quietly in his arms. Her yellow eyes observed the surroundings while her tail hung lazily to one side.","Noah looked down at her.","\"You know...\"","A grin appeared on his face.","\"If Arisha sees me carrying you around after you rejected her so many times that day, she’ll probably be jealous.\"","The cat stared at him unimpressed.","Noah laughed.","Then he turned toward the dormitory building.","With the injured black cat resting safely in his arms, he began walking back to his room."]},{"number":170,"title":"Chapter 170: New Cute Friend Of Noah","paragraphs":["Noah carefully placed the black cat on his bed. The mattress sank slightly beneath her small body.","\"There you go.\"","A gentle smile appeared on his face.","\"Rest here, dear.\"","The cat lazily stretched herself across the soft blanket. Her yellow eyes remained half-open while her black tail swayed slowly from side to side.","Noah walked toward his desk and retrieved some cotton along with a small bowl of clean water. Returning to the bed, he sat beside her.","\"Hmm.\"","His eyes landed on her injured leg.","\"I should clean that first.\"","He took some cotton and started to clean her.","The cat watched him cautiously but made no attempt to run away.","After carefully cleaning the wound, Noah leaned back slightly.","’I wonder if a healing potion would work on animals.’","He thought about it for a moment.","’Well... it should work.’","Reaching into his storage ring, he pulled out a basic healing potion. The glass vial glimmered under the room’s light.","Noah held it in front of the cat.","\"Hey.\"","He tapped the vial lightly. Trying to tell her that he was going to feed her this.","\"Open your mouth.\"","The cat blinked.","\"Meow~\"","Noah gently brought the opening of the vial toward her mouth. At the same moment, the cat flicked out her small pink tongue.","Noah slowly poured the potion. The cat swallowed it without much resistance.","It was surprising,’This cat is too smart.’","A few moments later, the wound on her leg began to heal visibly.","The torn skin slowly closed. The swelling faded. The injury disappeared entirely.","Noah’s eyes brightened.","\"Nice.\"","A satisfied smile appeared on his face. He gently stroked the top of her head. The cat immediately began purring.","\"Meow~\"","She seemed to enjoy his petting far more than she had enjoyed the medicine.","\"Good.\"","Noah scratched beneath her chin.","\"You’re completely healed now.\"","The cat lazily closed her eyes. For a moment, Noah simply watched her. Then he noticed something.","Her beautiful black fur wasn’t actually black anymore. It was dusty.","Leaves and dirt were caught in several places.","Noah frowned. He tilted his head.","\"You’re dirty.\"","The cat opened one eye.","Noah smiled. \"Let’s go clean you up.\"","The cat suddenly felt a very bad feeling. Before she could react, Noah lifted her into his arms.","\"Come on.\"","The cat stared up at him suspiciously. She had no idea where this human was taking her.","---","A few minutes later. Inside the bathroom.The cat’s yellow eyes slowly moved downward. Then she saw it.","There was water. A bucket filled with clean water. The realization hit her immediately. Her pupils shrank.","Noah smiled kindly. \"Now be a good girl, okay?\"","The cat froze.","\"I’ll wash you clean.\"","There was silence. For one brief moment. Then suddenly.","\"HISSSSSSS!!\"","The cat exploded.","\"MEOW! MEOW! MEOW!!\"","Her cries echoed throughout the bathroom.","Noah nearly dropped her.","\"Hey!\"","He quickly tightened his grip. \"Calm down!\"","The cat absolutely refused. All four paws began flailing wildly. Her tail puffed up.","Her fur stood on end. \"MEOW!!\"","\"There’s nothing dangerous here!\" Noah protested.","The cat clearly disagreed. The battle began.","Unfortunately for her... Her opponent was Noah. Someone who had recently fought demon.","Someone who trained daily.Someone physically far stronger than a normal cat.","Noah narrowed his eyes. \"Do you really think you can defeat me?\"","The cat answered with violence. A tiny paw smacked directly into his face.","Scratch.","\"Ouch!\"","Noah recoiled. The cat immediately tried to escape. She almost succeeded.","She almost had reach her escape route. Five seconds later she was back in his grasp.","\"No.\"","Noah pointed at her seriously. \"You’re taking a bath.\"","The cat looked horrified. And thus began thirty minutes of war.The bathroom echoed with endless cries.","\"MEOW!!\"","\"No.\"","\"MEOW!!\"","\"Stop struggling.\"","\"HISSSSS!\"","\"You’re literally covered in dirt.\"","The cat fought bravely. She scratched him. She even kicked him. She hissed. She attempted escape multiple times.","None of it worked.","Meanwhile, Noah thoroughly washed every part of her fur and body. By the end of it, she looked utterly defeated.","It almost felt like she was embarrassed every time Noah touched another part of her body while cleaning her.","Unfortunately, she was powerless to stop him. The battle ended with Noah victorious. The cat was not happy about it.","---","Back inside the room.","Noah immediately uncorked a healing potion. Then he drank it. Several scratches decorated his hands and face.","The wounds quickly healed. After finishing the potion, he turned toward the bed.","The cat sat there wrapped in a towel. Her fur was completely wet.","She looked miserable.","Noah couldn’t help laughing. \"You are one troublesome cat.\"","He sat beside her and began drying her carefully. The cat simply accepted her fate. She looked too tired to resist anymore.","As Noah gently rubbed the towel through her fur, a thoughtful expression appeared on his face.","\"Hmm. Since you are staying with me...\"","He tilted his head. \"I should give you a name.\"","The cat looked at him. \"Meow?\"","Noah completely ignored the fact that she had not agreed to become his pet. In his mind, that decision had already been made.","\"Should I call you Lisa?\"","He thought for a moment. \"Hmm... that’s a real girl’s name.\"","Then he nodded. \"But you’re cute.\"","A smile appeared on his face. \"And I like the name Lisa.\"","The cat stared at him unimpressed.","\"Or maybe Lalisa?\"","Noah continued seriously.","The cat looked even less impressed.","Noah remained determined. He spent several minutes considering names.","Finally, his eyes brightened. \"I got it.\"","He pointed at her like a scholar. \"Nancy!\"","The cat blinked.","\"Yes!\"","Noah looked at her with smirk.. \"Nancy!\"","He gently lifted her paws. \"My lovely Nancy!\"","\"Meow.\"","The cat’s expression remained utterly unimpressed. Her yellow eyes practically screamed disappointment. Unfortunately for her, she had absolutely no voting rights in this matter.","Her eyelids slowly drooped. She looked exhausted.","Noah immediately noticed.","\"Wait.\"","He poked her lightly.","\"Don’t sleep yet.\"","The cat opened one eye.","\"You need to eat first.\" His voice became gentle.","\"Come on.\" He carefully picked her up. \"Let’s go to the cafeteria.\"","A grin appeared on his face. \"There’s lots of food there.\"","The cat was lifted into his arms. \"And you’ll enjoy it.\"","As Noah walked toward the door, a mischievous thought appeared in his mind.’I should keep her hidden from Arisha for a while.’","A smile spread across his face. ’Let’s eat alone today.’","Today, Noah had gained a cute cat.","---","[A/N:Why did he got a cat? Hmm.. wait and see haha!!]"]},{"number":171,"title":"Chapter 171: Written Exam Over","paragraphs":["Ring!","The final bell rang throughout the academy.","Students immediately began leaving their classrooms as instructors collected the exam papers.","Today was the final day of the written examinations. Noah personally thought they had gone rather well.","Mana Theory.","Spell Casting.","Monster Ecology.","Basic Alchemy Fundamentals.","Tactics & Strategy.","Dungeon Studies.","Wilderness Survival.","Seven subjects.","An entire week of exams. Even Sunday hadn’t been spared. Thankfully, Noah had received help from smart person like Arisha.","Because of that, he felt confident about his results. After handing his paper to the supervising instructor, Noah left the classroom.","Stretching his arms, he smiled.","\"Finally.\"","A relieved sigh escaped him.","\"It’s over.\"","As he stepped outside, he immediately spotted two familiar figures. They were Lyria and Arisha. They were standing together near the corridor.","Noah waved. \"Hello, girls~\"","Both turned toward him. Arisha nodded calmly.","\"Hello, Noah.\" Lyria smiled softly. \"Hey, Noah.\" Her eyes studied him.","\"You look happy.\" A small laugh escaped her. \"Was the exam that easy for you?\"","Noah grinned. \"Yes.\"","He nodded. \"It was much better than I expected.\"","Then he pointed toward Arisha. \"And it’s all because of Arisha.\"","A grateful smile appeared on his face. \"She really helped me.\"","Lyria nodded.\"Yes, I know.\"","Then she looked at him. \"Honestly, I would have helped you too if you had asked.\"","Hearing that made Noah smile. \"Oh my.\"","He placed a hand over his chest. \"I am so lucky to have such a kind and caring friend.\"","Then he smiled brightly. \"Next time I’ll ask you to teach me—Owch!\"","Noah suddenly rubbed the side of his arm.","Arisha stood beside him with a disapproving expression. She had just pinched him.","Noah looked offended. \"Hey.\" He frowned. \"Why did you do that? I didn’t even say anything about you.\"","Arisha crossed her arms. \"Hah.\"","She raised an eyebrow. \"For real?\" Her eyes narrowed. \"I helped you so much.\"","She pointed at him. \"And now you’re talking about asking someone else?\"","Noah shrugged. \"So what?\"","A teasing grin appeared on his face. \"Lyria is much gentler and sweeter.\"","\"This bastard.\" Arisha muttered.","Beside them, a faint blush appeared on Lyria’s cheeks after hearing compliments from Noah.","Then Noah added, \"Besides, you aren’t teaching me for free.\"","His eyes narrowed suspiciously. \"You said you’d ask for something in return.\"","Arisha blinked.\"Oh.\"","She genuinely seemed to have forgotten. \"Right.\"","Then a slow smirk appeared on her face. \"Good thing you reminded me.\"","\"Tch!\"","Noah clicked his tongue. Immediately regretting his words.","\"What are you going to ask, Arisha?\"","Lyria asked curiously.","Arisha thought for a moment. Then her eyes narrowed. \"Tell me, Noah.\"","A suspicious expression appeared on her face. \"You’re hiding something from us.\"","Noah frowned. \"Hiding something?\" He looked completely innocent. \"Me?\"","He shook his head. \"I’m not hiding anything.\"","His acting skills remained flawless. Nobody could tell whether he was speaking the truth or lying.","Arisha wasn’t convinced. \"Hmm.\"","Her eyes narrowed further. \"I’ve noticed that you’ve been avoiding eating with us in the cafeteria.\"","Noah’s smile almost twitched.","’The hell? I only did that a few times. Most of the time I just bought food elsewhere. She’s dangerous.’","He maintained his honest expression. This much of a pressure won’t let his mask of honesty slip away.","\"Hey.\"","He raised both hands. \"I only did that a few times.\"","\"Yes.\"","Arisha nodded. \"A few times.\" Then she stared directly into his eyes. \"But you did. Why did you do that?\"","Noah calmly met her gaze. His expression never changed. Lyria quietly watched the battle.","Just then some one came. \"Hey, guys! What are you doing?\"","A familiar voice suddenly interrupted. The voice was something Noah was waiting for. He immediately turned around to see the perosn who came like a savior.","His savior had arrived.","There he was standing leonard. Beside him were Damien, Kaelan, and Emma. The group was as always together.","Noah almost looked emotional.","\"Oh, Leo.\"","He pointed at each of them.","\"Kael, Damn And Em.You all arrived at the perfect time. I was waiting for you guys.\"","Emma frowned.","\"What the hell is Em?\" She didn’t like what he just call her.","Damien raised an eyebrow.","\"And who’s Damn?\" Nor did Damien like what Noah just call him.","Leonard shrugged, not bothered by it.","\"Well, Leo is fine.\" His name was good one.","Kaelan nodded. \"Kael is fine too.\"","Noah grinned teasingly. \"Anyways.\"","He pointed toward Arisha and Lyria. \"I was just flirting with Arisha and Lyria.\" A sweet smile appeared on his face. \"Nothing much.\"","\"Fuck this bastard.\"","Leonard immediately cursed. \"He’s not even trying to hide it anymore.\"","Kaelan sighed. \"It’s not new.\"","Damien groaned. \"Noah...\"","Then Emma pointed at him. \"Hey!\" Her eyes widened. \"You’re doing it again? Why are you flirting with Lyria and Arisha?!\"","Out of the four newcomers, only Leonard and Emma gave him the reaction he wanted.","Lyria quickly waved her hands.","\"Guys.\" She laughed softly. \"Noah is just joking.\"","Her smile remained gentle. \"Why are you taking him seriously?\"","Noah nodded like a smart perosn. Then he turned toward Leonard. \"Hah.\"","A knowing smile appeared on his face. \"If you want, I can give you some good tips, Leo.\"","Leonard froze. \"W-Wait.\"","His eyes widened. \"Really?\"","\"Of course.\" Noah nodded confidently. \"I bet you want romance too.\" Then he placed a hand on Leonard’s shoulder.","\"I can help you.\"","Leonard looked touched. \"Damn! \"Noah, you’re the best!\"","He pointed at Noah. \"Hehe~\"","Noah grinned. \"Of course I’m the best.\" Then he glanced toward Damien. \"But not Damn.\"","Damien frowned. But wisely chose not to respond. Experience had taught him that arguing with Noah rarely ended well.","Meanwhile, Noah could still feel a suspicious gaze from behind. Arisha was still watching him. Still suspicious.","Noah immediately decided to change the topic. \"Hey, guys.\"","He looked around at everyone. \"Do any of you have an idea what our practical exam might be?\"","His expression became curious. \"You know...\" A grin appeared. \"It’s much more important than the written exams.\"","---","[A/N:Hello guys! I said this in my other novel, now time for here You know I had created my kofi account months ago,when I started to write my first novel. But forgot about it. Now that I remember. I thought I should tell you. Well so in short if you want to support me outside of WN you can do it via kofi. I put link in synopsis of my both novels. You know it’s better to get direct money rather than gift since more than half if it goes to app and other things. We get nearly half or might be less. So if you ever wish to gift my novel, it’s better to donate by kofi rather then giving so many coins. Link is also available in my server.","Also coins are acceptable if going to kofi is too hard work. I know since I am lazy myself.","Hehe~ bye bye!"]},{"number":172,"title":"Chapter 172: ’I can’t bring myself to harm you.’","paragraphs":["As the group started walking toward the cafeteria, the conversation naturally shifted toward the upcoming practical exam.","Leonard scratched the back of his head and shrugged. \"I have no idea what this practical exam might be about.\"","Beside him, Damien shook his head.","\"Me neither.\"","Noah looked at both of them before clicking his tongue.","\"Tch. You people are supposed to be the talents of this generation, and you didn’t even bother searching what the first semester exam was for first-year students last year?\"","Kaelan glanced at him calmly.","\"I don’t need to do that.\"","His expression remained completely indifferent. \"Whatever they throw at me, I’m ready for it.\"","Noah nodded. He already understood how these top-ranked students thought.","They were confident in their abilities. Whether it was monsters, survival, or combat, they believed they could overcome it.","Leonard suddenly grinned.","\"Of course. I’m the same.\"","He folded his arms behind his head. \"It’s more fun to face the unknown.\"","Noah sighed. \"You battle maniacs.\"","Then he turned toward Arisha. \"What do you think?\"","Arisha looked at him.","Or rather, she stared at him.","The kind of stare a wife might give her husband after catching him hiding something suspicious.","Her golden eyes narrowed slightly. \"You still haven’t told me what you’re hiding.\"","Noah immediately looked away. \"I don’t know what you’re talking about.\"","\"Hm.\"","Arisha clearly didn’t believe him.","\"But for now, I’ll let it slide.\"","Then she shifted the conversation.","\"Last year’s first semester practical exam was Battle Survival.\"","Everyone listened.","\"All first-year students were placed inside a forest. They had to fight and eliminate each other.\"","\"A battle royale?\" Noah asked.","Arisha nodded.","\"The last student standing received the highest score and many bonus points.\"","Noah rubbed his chin thoughtfully.","\"Hmm.\"","His eyes narrowed.","\"This year might be different then.\"","\"Most likely.\"","Arisha agreed.","Lyria, who had been quietly listening until now, turned toward Noah.","\"Do you want to become Rank One?\"","Her soft voice carried genuine curiosity.","Damien also raised an eyebrow.","He seemed interested in Noah’s answer.","Before Noah could speak, Emma immediately interrupted.","\"Him?\"","She pointed at Noah.","\"First Rank?\"","Emma shook her head.","\"That’s impossible.\"","Noah completely ignored her.","Emma was Damien’s problem. Not his. After all, Damien was the one who spent the most time with her.","Noah thought for a moment before answering.","\"Well...\"","A small smile appeared on his face.","\"Not Rank One exactly.\"","His expression turned serious.","\"But I do want to be in the Top Ten.\"","Lyria smiled gently.","\"That’s a nice goal.\"","\"Right?\"","Noah nodded.","Then a thought suddenly crossed his mind. \"If it ends up being a battle royale...\"","He turned toward Lyria.","A warm smile appeared on his face.","\"We’ll fight together.\"","Lyria blinked.","Noah continued speaking naturally. \"I can’t bring myself to harm you.\"","His voice was calm and sincere. \"So let’s form an alliance.\"","His smile widened slightly. \"Together, we can conquer it. It doesn’t matter what kind of exam it is.\"","His gentle expression and caring voice made the atmosphere strangely quiet.","The rest of the group stared at him. Leonard looked baffled. Emma looked horrified. Kaelan looked mildly impressed.","Damien simply stared in amusement.","Arisha rolled her eyes.A tired sigh escaped her lips.","Meanwhile, Lyria’s cheeks slowly turned red.","She quickly looked away. For some reason, whenever Noah spoke to her like that, she became flustered far too easily.","Just then something happened.","Pinch.","\"Owch!\"","Noah immediately rubbed the side of his arm.","Arisha had pinched him again.","He turned toward her with disbelief. \"Why do you always do that?\"","Arisha folded her arms. \"Don’t flirt so openly.\"","Noah looked offended. \"I was being sincere.\"","\"That’s somehow worse.\"","\"Tch.\"","Noah rubbed the sore spot. Then he looked toward Lyria again.","\"Fine.\"","He nodded dramatically. \"Next time I’ll flirt with her when we’re alone.\"","Lyria’s face instantly turned bright red.","\"NOAH!\"","Without thinking, she punched his shoulder. Unfortunately, the punch contained absolutely no strength.","It felt more like a gentle tap. For a pure and gentle girl like Lyria, she couldn’t hit Noah aggressively using her powers. This was already the limit.","Noah laughed.","Meanwhile Leonard looked envious.","Kaelan couldn’t care less. Emma looked like she wanted to strangle Noah.","Damien sat somewhere between amusement and irritation.","The group continued walking until they finally reached the cafeteria.","Students filled the large hall. The smell of food drifted through the air.","Many tables were already occupied. As Noah searched for a place to sit, his eyes suddenly landed on two familiar figures.","Ragnar and Draven. The two of them were carrying trays piled with food.","However, both looked unusually depressed. Their shoulders drooped.Their faces looked gloomy.","Noah immediately raised a hand.","\"Hey, Ragnar! Draven!\"","The duo turned around. The moment they spotted Noah, their expressions somehow became even sadder.","Noah blinked. \"What happened to you two?\"","Ragnar let out a long sigh.","Draven looked toward the ceiling as though questioning life itself. Both of them slowly walked toward Noah and the others.","Whatever had happened, it clearly wasn’t good.","\"Noah...\" Ragnar looked at him with a tired expression. \"You’re asking what happened?\"","He pointed at Noah dramatically. \"You already know what happened.\"","A painful look appeared on his face. \"All of those written exams...\"","Beside him, Draven slowly nodded. His face looked even more miserable. \"They were scary...\"","He paused. Then he added in a grave tone, \"They were scarier than my mother.\"","The entire group fell silent. Nobody knew what to say to that.","Noah looked at the two of them for a moment. Then he gently patted both of their shoulders. \"Don’t worry.\"","A reassuring smile appeared on his face. \"I know you two will pass.\"","His voice carried confidence. \"I believe in you guys.\"","\"N-Noah!\"","Ragnar’s eyes trembled. Beside him, Draven also looked touched.","\"Noah...\"","Ragnar nodded firmly. \"Thanks for the encouragement.\"","Draven placed a hand over his chest. \"You are a true friend.\"","Noah simply smiled. After that, the group collected their food and moved toward a large table."]},{"number":173,"title":"Chapter 173: Two Lovers","paragraphs":["With Ragnar and Draven joining them, the seating arrangement became slightly complicated.","Noah glanced around.","Ragnar, Draven, Leonard, and Kaelan sat on one side of the table.","On the opposite side sat Damien, Emma, and Lyria.","Noah looked toward the empty seat beside Lyria. Without hesitation, he walked over and sat down.","He made sure to claim the seat before Arisha could.","Arisha arrived a moment later. Seeing Noah already sitting there, she raised an eyebrow.","However, she didn’t comment on it. Instead, she sat on Noah’s other side.","The group finally began eating. As Noah picked up his fork, his thoughts drifted back toward the practical exam.","’We’ll probably receive all the details on our phones this evening.’","His curiosity only grew. ’I really want to know what kind of exam it will be.’","Then his gaze landed on Leonard. A thoughtful expression appeared on his face.","\"Leonard.\"","Leonard looked up.","\"Hm?\"","Noah pointed at him. \"You should let me help you.\"","Leonard narrowed his eyes suspiciously.","\"What do you mean?\"","\"First.\" Noah leaned slightly forward. \"Tell me.\"","His expression turned serious. \"Do you have a girl you like? Or maybe a fiancée?\"","Leonard immediately shook his head.","\"No.\" His answer came instantly. \"I don’t have either.\"","\"Really?\"","Noah looked surprised. \"Not even a girl you think you might like?\"","Leonard thought for a moment. Then he shook his head again.","\"Hmm.\" His expression remained calm. \"I’ve never really focused on that.\"","He shrugged. \"After all, I spend most of my time training.\"","\"The hell?\" Noah stared at him.","\"Then why do you always get angry whenever I spend time with Lyria or Arisha?\"","Leonard immediately pointed at Noah. \"That’s exactly what I mean!\"","His voice rose slightly. \"I never cared about any of this before.\"","Then he sighed dramatically. \"But after watching you...\"","He shook his head. \"I started thinking about it.\"","A serious expression appeared on his face. \"I’m a young man too.\" He folded his arms.","\"I also need romance.\"","The two boys immediately began discussing strange relationship topics. The others wisely focused on eating.","Well... Almost everyone.","Though Draven looked curious. He glanced between Noah, Lyria, and Arisha.","Then he asked, \"Hmm.\" His expression became thoughtful. \"So not only Arisha...\"","He looked toward Lyria. \"Lyria is also Noah’s lover?\"","Cough!","Lyria instantly choked on her food. Her shoulders shook as she began coughing.","\"Cough! Cough!\"","\"Oh!\"","Noah quickly turned toward her.","\"Lyria.\"","His expression filled with concern. \"What are you doing?\"","He gently patted her back. \"Eat slowly.\"","His voice softened. \"Calm down.\"","He continued rubbing her back. \"Take a normal breath.\"","After a few moments, Lyria finally stopped coughing. Her eyes had become slightly watery. A faint redness covered her cheeks.","Noah immediately grabbed the glass of water beside her. Then he carefully held it toward her lips.","\"Here.\"","His voice remained gentle. \"Drink.\"","Lyria looked up at him. Her pink eyes were slightly teary. Her cheeks grew even redder.","Without saying anything, she quietly drank the water. The entire table watched the scene unfold.","Everyone looked slightly stunned. Even Arisha blinked. She glanced at Noah with amusement. The way he was acting was surprisingly too caring. She never thought he could be so much caring.","Once Lyria recovered, Noah finally relaxed. \"You should eat more slowly.\"","He sighed. \"Why were you eating so fast?\"","Noah thought to himself. ’Am I doing too much?’","Then he glanced at Lyria. ’But it’s fun teasing her and seeing her cute reactions.’","A moment later his expression softened. ’Although this time she genuinely worried me.’","Lyria wanted to yell at him. She really did. But instead, she simply glared at him.","Her eyes clearly said, ’Don’t act like you don’t know why this happened.’","Noah pretended not to understand.","Meanwhile, Draven nodded seriously.","\"Wow.\"","His eyes shone with admiration. \"Noah.\"","He gave him a thumbs-up. \"You are a real man.\"","Then he added, \"Caring for your woman so much.\"","A moment later, Draven paused. His gaze slowly shifted toward Arisha.","\"However...\"","He pointed toward her. \"You should also take care of your other woman.\"","His expression became wise. \"Before she gets jealous.\"","Immediately, everyone’s eyes turned toward Arisha.","Arisha, who had been looking at Noah a few seconds ago, calmly returned her attention to her food.","Then she frowned. \"Why would I be jealous?\"","\"Haha.\" Leonard laughed awkwardly.","\"Right. Noah is just joking.\"","He waved his hand. \"It’s not like they’re actually his lovers.\"","Damien nodded. \"Yes.\" His expression remained calm. \"We know that.\"","Emma rubbed the bridge of her nose. \"No way.\"","She sighed. \"They would never like him.\"","Then she added, \"And how would someone even date two women in this era?\"","Her expression looked completely unconvinced. \"Having multiple partners is extremely rare nowadays.\"","She shrugged. \"It usually only happens because of political reasons.\"","Leonard nodded. \"I already know that.\"","Then Regnar, he pointed at Draven. \"Only Draven had the wrong idea.\"","\"What?!\"","Draven’s eyes widened. His entire worldview shook.","\"You mean...\" His gaze bounced between Noah, Lyria, and Arisha.","\"Lyria and Arisha aren’t Noah’s women?\"","The barbarian man looked genuinely shocked.","Noah couldn’t help chuckling.","Then without any warning, he extended his arm toward Arisha. His hand landed on top of her head.","Pat.","He gently stroked her soft hair.","Arisha’s entire body stiffened instantly. The spoon she had been lifting toward her mouth froze in midair.","Noah smiled warmly. \"I was wrong, Arisha.\"","He continued patting her head. \"How could I neglect you?\"","A teasing grin appeared on his face. \"Don’t be jealous, my dear.\"","His fingers gently ruffled her hair. \"You are a good girl after all.\"","Aisha’s ears turned slightly pink.","While Noah beyond happy. ’Take this!! I have been waiting for this opportunity! You have pat my head multiple time now it’s my time.’","\"Do you want me to do anything for you? Just tell me?\"","Now once again everyone were shocked.","Draven just nodded with understanding. \"I was right.\"","Arisha bite her lower lip and turned her head to face him.","She watched his happy face and then said, \"If you want to calm me down... tell me what were you hiding for few days?\"","And no way Arisha going to back down."]},{"number":174,"title":"Chapter 174: What’s This Exam Going to be about?","paragraphs":["\"Goodness, Arisha. You’re still on that?\"","Noah looked at her helplessly.","Arisha crossed her arms and nodded firmly. \"Yes.\"","A small smirk appeared on her face. \"I won’t back off until I learn the truth.\"","At that moment, the scene of Noah patting Arisha’s head was so shocking that almost nobody registered what she had actually asked.","Lyria looked completely surprised. Emma looked like she wanted to slam her head into the table.","Draven’s respect for Noah continued to rise.","Ragnar simply shook his head.","The others were equally baffled.","Noah let out a long sigh. \"Hah...\"","Then he raised both hands in surrender. \"Okay, okay.\"","His expression turned resigned. He waved his hand dismissively. \"I’ll tell you. It’s nothing special.\"","Then he pointed at her. \"I’ll tell you later, okay?\"","Arisha immediately looked victorious. A satisfied smirk appeared on her face.","She nodded. \"Good. That’s what I wanted to hear.\"","Noah withdrew his hand from her head with a defeated expression. As he did, he noticed someone staring at his hand.","Lyria, her pink eyes were fixed on it. Noticing her gaze, Noah tilted his head.","\"You want me to pat you too?\"","Lyria instantly turned bright red. \"N-No!\"","She shook her head rapidly. \"No!\"","Her rejection came so quickly that it only made Noah grin.","Just like that, the strange but friendly lunch finally came to an end.","After lunch, Noah spent some time walking around the campus.","Eventually, he headed toward the training grounds and trained for several hours.","Only after exhausting himself did he finally return to his dormitory room.","The moment he opened the door, his expression softened.","Nancy was there. The secret he had been hiding from Arisha. To be honest, there wasn’t really any reason to hide it.","He would probably tell her sooner or later.","Most likely, Arisha would immediately come to visit. Nothing much.","Or more accurately. She would come to meet Nancy.","He looked at the cat. The proud little black cat was lying elegantly on the bed.","When Noah entered the room, she raised her head curiously.","\"Meow?\"","Noah smiled.","First, he went to take a warm bath.","After washing away the sweat from training, he returned wearing comfortable casual clothes.","Then he jumped onto the bed. \"So nice.\"","He stretched comfortably. Noah lay on his back while staring at the ceiling and massaging his sore muscles.","Then he reached out and grabbed Nancy.","The cat was easily lifted into his arms.","Without hesitation, Noah kissed her forehead.","Then another kiss and another and another.","\"Meow!!\"","Nancy immediately began protesting. \"Meow!! Meow!!\"","The cat clearly hated the kisses. She struggled to escape. Unfortunately, Noah ignored all objections.","\"I missed you, Nancy.\" He smiled brightly. \"Did you miss me too?\"","He gently placed her on his chest. Nancy sat there while glaring at him with pure feline rage.","\"Meow! Meow!\"","\"Hehe.\"","Noah laughed. \"So you missed me too.\"","He began petting her head.","Of course... That wasn’t what Nancy meant at all.","Eventually, the room became quiet. Nancy settled comfortably on Noah’s chest.","For a few peaceful moments, neither of them moved.","But just the another sound came.","Ring!","A sharp notification sound echoed through the room. It was the unique alert tone used by the Academy application installed on every student’s phone.","Noah frowned.Then he grabbed the device from beside him.","After unlocking it, a crimson notification banner immediately appeared on the screen.","[NOTICE: FIRST-YEAR SEMESTER EXAM SPECIFICATIONS RELEASED]","His eyes sharpened. Immediately opening the notice, Noah began reading.","The official document appeared beneath the Academy crest.","CAMPUS-WIDE DIRECTIVE: THE WILDERNESS RACE","[Overview:]","All first-year students are hereby notified that the upcoming Semester Exam will consist of a live-combat survival race.","Students will be deployed at an undisclosed location, which will be revealed on the day of the examination.","Their objective will be to navigate the terrain and reach the Beacon.","[Duration & Survival:]","The exam will run continuously for 48 hours (2 days).","Students are permitted to carry standard-issue weapons and any necessary potions.","[Point Distribution Breakdown:]","Further details will be provided before the examination begins.","This notification has been issued to allow students sufficient time to prepare and train in advance, as the exam may involve danger.","[Final Evaluation:]","Your final semester grade will be determined by the total points registered from all exams.","Noah slowly scrolled through the remaining information. The blue glow of the screen reflected in his eyes.","After finishing, he lowered the phone onto his chest.","Then he stared at the ceiling. His mind immediately began constructing strategies.","\"The hell?\"","He frowned.","\"They only gave half the information.\"","A sigh escaped him. Even so... The notice was enough. Noah already had a rough idea of what the exam would involve.","’Since it’s a race...’","His eyes narrowed. ’There will definitely be monsters. We’ll probably earn points by killing them.’","A thoughtful expression appeared on his face. ’And students will likely be able to steal points from each other by eliminating opponents.’","That was common in these kinds of examinations. Noah sighed again. Now he was more interested in the dangers waiting for them.","’The next Act of the story should be the semester exam.’","His eyes drifted toward the window. ’It’s on Friday. Today is Sunday. They’ve given us enough time to prepare.’","He closed his eyes. ’I already absorbed those cores I got from Travis.’","For now, there wasn’t much else to do. Noah wrapped his arms around Nancy, giving her a hug. The cat immediately looked offended.","Then he took a small nap.","--","The next day, Noah visited several shops. He purchased healing potions. Mana recovery potions. Stamina recovery potions. And several other useful supplies.","After all he wanted to do as good as possible and also be ready for whatever danger woukd fall upon him at the exam.","After finishing his shopping, he decided to head toward the training grounds.","However as he walked through one of the academy corridors, he suddenly noticed someone standing near a large window.","His steps slowed as he saw that person."]},{"number":175,"title":"Chapter 175: Second Petal – Still Surface Cut","paragraphs":["The woman wore a purple shirt with the sleeves rolled neatly up to her forearms. Her long sky-blue hair was tied into a neat bun.","Several loose strands framed her beautiful face. A black pencil skirt wrapped around her figure.","High heels made her appear even taller.","Around 183 centimeters. Nearly the same height as Noah.","The woman was none other than Morgana.","Their head instructor.","Noah immediately walked toward her. \"Hello, Instructor Morgana.\"","Hearing his voice, Morgana turned her head. Her calm amethyst eyes met his. Her expression was relaxed.","The usual strictness she carried wasn’t present right now.","For Noah, Morgana was practically a hero. He still remembered the day she had saved him when several main characters had been chasing him down.","He genuinely respected her. And Morgana could easily see that admiration in his eyes.","\"Noah?\"","She looked at him calm expression.","\"Going to the training ground, I assume?\"","Noah nodded. \"Yes.\"","His expression turned serious. \"I need to practice as much as possible for the upcoming exam.\"","Morgana nodded approvingly. \"Good. Your progress has been remarkable among all students in our class.\"","Her gaze remained steady. \"I have high expectations from you.\"","Noah smiled softly. \"I am very glad to hear that.\"","Then he added, \"I’ll do my best to rank within the Top Ten.\"","\"Haha.\" Morgana chuckled lightly.","\"I like your confidence.\"","A small smile appeared on her face.","\"And your dedication.\"","Then she added, \"You’re nothing like what others say.\"","Noah felt strangely happy hearing those words.","\"Hm, Instructor.\"","He tilted his head \"What were you doing here?\"","\"Nothing.\"","Morgana looked out the window. A tired look briefly crossed her face.","\"I was working for long.\"","She sighed softly.","\"So I decided to get some fresh air.\"","Noah nodded. \"Oh. As expected.\"","A smile appeared on his face. \"You really work hard.\"","His voice was sincere. \"You are amazing.\"","Morgana raised one eyebrow. Amusement flashed in her eyes. She was famous for being ruthless and brutal.","Most students showed fear toward her.","Yet this student continued showering her with compliments any time he get chance.","Even her disciple, Damien sometimes cursed her training methods. Never trying to compliment her so much.","Meanwhile Noah only ever said good things.","She had personally beaten him during training many times.","Yet somehow he still admired her. \"Hey.\"","A faint smile appeared on her lips. \"Compliments won’t get you anywhere with me.\"","Noah laughed. \"Hahaha. I know.\"","Then his expression became genuine.","\"But Instructor, I’m honestly happy that you’re our head instructor.\"","His eyes carried respect.","\"I like your strictness. I like your ruthlessness. Those things help students grow stronger faster.\"","Then he shrugged. \"So I’m just being honest.\"","\"Oh boy...\" For the first time, Morgana’s smile became softer one.","Then she narrowed her eyes. \"What do you want?\"","Her expression turned suspicious. \"You’ve been talking far too nicely and sweet.\"","She crossed her arms. \"I can’t help but think you want something.\"","\"No!\"","Noah immediately denied it. \"Absolutely not.\"","Then he paused. \"But...\"","A sheepish smile appeared on his face. \"If you insist on thinking that way...\"","He scratched his cheek. \"I was hoping you could train me more.\"","Morgana blinked. \"Now that was unexpected, Noah. You also had ask this before. \"","She stared at him for several moments. Then she thought about it. Finally, she nodded.","\"Okay. You can come to the training grounds around five in the evening.\"","She continued calmly.\"I teach Damien at that time.You can join with him.\"","Noah’s eyes brightened. \"Oh?\"","A huge smile appeared on his face. \"Thank you!\"","Then he added enthusiastically, \"You’re the best instructor.\"","\"Hmm.\" Morgana returned to her usual calm expression.","\"You really do talk too sweet.\"","Noah simply nodded. Then another thought appeared in his mind.","\"Instructor.\"","He straightened.","\"Could you have a small session with me right now?\"","His eyes shone with anticipation. \"I’d like you to see my progress.\"","Morgana considered it. After a moment, she nodded.","\"I have some free time.\"","She pushed herself away from the window.","\"I can help you.\"","Then she turned around.","\"Let’s go.\"","Without waiting, she started walking toward the training grounds.","Noah immediately followed after her. While doing his absolute best not to look at her swaying hips.","---","The training hall echoed with the sounds of clashing steel.","Clang!","Clang!","Clang!","Noah’s sword collided against Morgana’s wooden training blade again and again. Each impact sent vibrations through his arms.","His breathing had long become ragged.","Sweat soaked his clothes.","His muscles burned from exhaustion.","Yet he continued attacking.","Morgana stood across from him with her usual calm expression. Despite sparring with him for quite a while, not a single drop of sweat could be seen on her forehead.","The difference between them was simply too great.","Clang!","Noah swung again.","Morgana casually redirected the attack and tapped his shoulder with her blade.","A clean hit.","Noah staggered backward before finally losing balance.","Thud!","He fell onto the floor while gripping his sword tightly.","\"Hah... hah...\"","His chest rose and fell heavily. Morgana looked down at him with her arms folded.","For a moment she remained silent before speaking.","\"Is this enough for today?\"","Noah wiped the sweat from his forehead and shook his head.","\"Yes... it is. Thank you for your help.\"","She nodded.","\"No need to thank. You really improve. I will go now then.\"","\"Yes Instructor.\"","Morgana left Noah behind.","When she step out of the training hall.","Her eyes narrowed with interest.","Just now she clearly felt it while fighting him.","Noah was at awakened core, high stage.","Before the incident that happened in forest of Oakhaven city. She had notice it that Noah was at awakened core, low stage.","But suddnely he crossed two sub ranks withing month.","That was very unusual.","She could accept that a perosn crossing one sub rank within month. Like Damien. But two?","This really made her surprised.","\"Let’s see how good he does in exam.\" She muttered with curiosity.","---","Meanwhile Noah slowly stood up. His legs felt heavy. His arms trembled slightly from fatigue.","Even so, he tightened his grip around the sword.","He now wanted to try his new second form of blade art that he has been training for three months.","This was the second form of the Frozen Lotus Blade Art.","[Second Petal – Still Surface Cut]","His proficiency was still low at this.","Around thirty percent.He closed his eyes. The noisy training hall seemed to fade away.","His breathing gradually slowed.","There was exhaustion and there was excitement. The desire performed as good as possible.","Then everything disappeared.One by one, his emotions sank into stillness.","There was silence. Only the sword remained. Only the path of the blade existed.","Noah’s eyes narrowed slightly. The atmosphere around him changed. It became more cold.","He was calm. He was Still. Like the surface of a frozen lake.","Noah slowly opened his eyes. There was no emotion inside them.","Right now he was emotionless.","There was only focus. Then he moved.","Slash!","The sword cut through the air in a simple horizontal strike. The movement looked ordinary.","Almost disappointingly simple.","Yet the instant the blade completed its motion. A distortion rippled through the air.","A thin white line appeared for the a moment.","Shhhh!","An invisible slash shot forward. The compressed freezing force traveled across the hall and struck a training dummy positioned nearly twenty meters away.","For a second nothing happened.","Crack.","A deep cut suddenly opened across the dummy. Frost rapidly spread from the wound.","Ice crawled over the wooden surface.","Crack!","Crack!","The entire upper half of the dummy became frozen.","A moment later it split apart cleanly. The top section slid from the lower half and crashed onto the floor.","Boom!","Silence filled the hall."]}]);
